{"level":30,"time":1776445226693,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WUzF6kVvBcGUQ3vynP78rp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, so I have the grouping file. This is a comprehensive guide about site feature clearances from overhead electric lines in Austin. The grouping is `el-md-exp` and this is file `1.md`, so the grouping ID is `1`.\n\nLet me break this down:\n\n**Description**: Reviews clearance requirements between overhead electric distribution/transmission facilities and proposed site features (buildings, fences, walls, etc.)\n\n**Key Thresholds**:\n- 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead primary, neutral, and secondary conductors\n- 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n- 16 feet minimum vertical clearance for driveways without truck traffic\n- 18 feet minimum vertical clearance for roads/streets/alleys with truck traffic\n- 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors for trees (utility compatible required)\n- 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors for trees (utility compatible required)\n- 10-foot radial clearance for construction working clearances\n\n**Documents to Review**: Site plan sheets, building elevations, section/profile exhibits, survey data, landscape plans, utility plans, cover sheet\n\n**47 checklist items** (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47)\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check applicability - does this site have overhead electric facilities?\n2. Review the site plan data to understand what facilities exist\n3. Evaluate each of the 47 checklist items\n\nLet me start by reading the project README and facts.md to understand what's on this site.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8163,"cache_read_input_