{"level":30,"time":1776445227456,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BbE7f3HyyewScSLwiYCQHK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. I now understand the grouping. This is about transformer pad clearances and location requirements. Let me understand the key aspects:\n\n**Description**: Transformer pad spatial and location requirements - clearances from buildings, structures, underground utilities, overhead lines, trees, property location restrictions.\n\n**Key Thresholds**:\n- 10 feet hot-stick use area (access door) to open area or building\n- 15 feet when facing confined space\n- 5 feet from removable fences (with operators/controls)\n- 3 feet from removable fences (without operators/controls)\n- 5 feet from brick/masonry buildings\n- 12 feet from non-brick/masonry buildings (for oil-filled equipment)\n- 2 feet from sidewalks\n- 20 feet from fire escapes (oil-filled equipment)\n- 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground from overhead distribution\n- 15-foot radius from overhead distribution conductors\n- 12 inches minimum from other utilities\n- 24-36 inches from gas lines\n- 5 feet from Austin Water infrastructure\n- Trees 10 feet lateral from pad, shrubs 10 feet from access door, 5 feet from other sides\n- Root barriers for trees within 20 feet\n- 4-inch bollards when pad within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas\n- Transformer pads 100% on private property\n- Electrical routing 100% on private property\n- Transformer easements required\n- 35-foot vertical clearance for niches\n- Proper orientation and documentation for various clearances\n\n**Checklist Items**: There are 39 items covering various aspects of transformer pad placement and clearances.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check applicability - does this site have transformer pads?\n2. Research what's on the site plan\n3. Evaluate eac