{"level":30,"time":1776445241713,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVgKR5s7r2cNcLGH98oV26","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 4 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This is a detailed site plan drawing showing an existing conditions survey. It includes property lines, buildings (existing slabs), trees, fences, utilities, and topographic contours. Key features include 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' on the left side, 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION' in the center, and 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS' on the right.\n     4→\n     5→The drawing represents an existing conditions survey of a property. It features detailed topographic contours, various trees marked with identifiers (e.g., +4046, +4047), and a large structure footprint labeled 'SLAB F.F.E.-686.8' within 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION VOL. 73, PG. 76 P.R.T.C.TX'. The property is bordered by 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' to the west. Various utility lines, fences (chain link, wood, crete), and easements are depicted. Adjacent properties include 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS VOL. 64, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX' and a property labeled 'WILLIAM LANCE COMSBIE, JR. (1.957 AC.) VOL. 5139, PG. 563 D.R.T.C.TX'. A scale bar and north arrow are present on the left side.\n     6→\n     7→## Block 3: notes — Certification statement and signature of the Registered Professional Land Surveyor who performed the survey.\n     8→\n     9→THIS SURVEY WAS PERFORMED WITHOUT THE BENEFIT OF A CURRENT\n    10→TITLE COMMITMENT AND THERE MAY BE EASEMENTS, BUILDING LINES,\n    11→CONDITIONS, OR RESTRICTIONS OF RECORD NOT SHOWN OR NOTED\n    12→HEREON.\n    13→DATE OF SURVEY: DECEMBER 27, 2024\n    14→RYAN T. LENZ\n    15→REGISTERED PROFESSIONAL LAND SURVEYOR NO. 7624\n    16→SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\n    17→TBPELS FIRM No. 10089000\n    18→4150 FREIDRICH LANE, SUITE A-1\n    19→AUSTIN, TEXAS 78744\n    20→(512) 443-1174\n    21→\n    22→## Block 4: notes — List of cities where Bleyl Engineering operates.\n    23→\n    24→Austin Bryan Conroe Houston\n    25→\n    26→## Block 5: notes — Information regarding the coordinate system and bearing basis used for the survey.\n    27→\n    28→BEARING BASIS:\n    29→BEARINGS, DISTANCES AND COORDINATES ARE\n    30→BASED ON THE TEXAS COORDINATE SYSTEM\n    31→OF 1983 (NAD83) CENTRAL ZONE, GRID.\n    32→\n    33→## Block 6: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n    34→\n    35→JOB NUMBER: 20240953\n    36→\n    37→## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n    38→\n    39→LEGEND\n    40→\n    41→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n    42→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n    43→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n    44→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n    45→- MAG NAIL SET\n    46→- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n    47→- NAIL FOUND\n    48→- 60D NAIL FOUND\n    49→- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n    50→- IRON PIPE FOUND\n    51→- MAG NAIL FOUND\n    52→- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n    53→- WATER METER\n    54→- WATER VALVE\n    55→- SPRINKLE FOUND\n    56→- WOOD FENCE\n    57→- UTILITY POLE\n    58→- WIRE FENCE\n    59→- LIGHT POLE\n    60→- CRETE FENCE\n    61→- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n    62→- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n    63→- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n    64→- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n    65→- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n    66→- W.L. WATER LINE\n    67→- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n    68→- T.L. TOWN LOT\n    69→- C.I. CURB INLET\n    70→- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n    71→- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n    72→- - CLEAN-OUT\n    73→- - FIRE HYDRANT\n    74→- - AIR CONDITIONER\n    75→- - SIGN POST\n    76→- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n    77→- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    78→- R.P.R.T.C.TX. REAL PROPERTY RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    79→- P.R.T.C.TX. PLAT RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    80→- D.R.T.C.TX. DEED RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    81→- T. TRAFFIC SIGN\n    82→- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n    83→- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n    84→\n    85→## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n    86→\n    87→TREE TABLE\n    88→| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n    89→|---|---|---|\n    90→| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n    91→| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n    92→| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n    93→| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n    94→| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n    95→| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n    96→| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n    97→| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n    98→| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n    99→| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n   100→| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n   101→| 4012 | 12\" | HACKBERRY |\n   102→| 4013 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n   103→| 4014 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n   104→| 4015 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n   105→| 4016 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   106→| 4017 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   107→| 4019 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   108→| 4022 | 24\" | PECAN |\n   109→| 4023 | 24\" | M |\n   110→| 4024 | 8\" | ELM |\n   111→| 4025 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n   112→| 4026 | 28\" | HACKBERRY |\n   113→| 4027 | 15\" | M |\n   114→| 4028 | 36\" | HACKBERRY |\n   115→| 4030 | 14\" | PECAN |\n   116→| 4031 | 16\" | LIVE OAK |\n   117→| 4032 | 18\" | LIVE OAK |\n   118→| 4033 | 11\" | ELM |\n   119→| 4034 | 20\" | CHINA BERRY |\n   120→| 4035 | 16\" | ELM |\n   121→| 4036 | 14\" | PECAN |\n   122→| 4037 | 11\" | ASH |\n   123→| 4038 | 20\" | HACKBERRY |\n   124→| 4040 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n   125→| 4041 | 13\" | ELM |\n   126→| 4042 | 34\" | LIVE OAK |\n   127→| 4043 | 15\" | LIVE OAK |\n   128→| 4044 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n   129→| 4045 | 20\" | LIVE OAK |\n   130→| 4046 | 17\" | LIVE OAK |\n   131→| 4047 | 16\" | PINE |\n   132→\n   133→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97c9d1ef-3ef8-4a72-b129-cbdede465e25","uuid":"c6c24b3a-ab42-4745-a57a-63c2b32c93d3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 4 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This is a detailed site plan drawing showing an existing conditions survey. It includes property lines, buildings (existing slabs), trees, fences, utilities, and topographic contours. Key features include 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' on the left side, 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION' in the center, and 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS' on the right.\n\nThe drawing represents an existing conditions survey of a property. It features detailed topographic contours, various trees marked with identifiers (e.g., +4046, +4047), and a large structure footprint labeled 'SLAB F.F.E.-686.8' within 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION VOL. 73, PG. 76 P.R.T.C.TX'. The property is bordered by 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' to the west. Various utility lines, fences (chain link, wood, crete), and easements are depicted. Adjacent properties include 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS VOL. 64, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX' and a property labeled 'WILLIAM LANCE COMSBIE, JR. (1.957 AC.) VOL. 5139, PG. 563 D.R.T.C.TX'. A scale bar and north arrow are present on the left side.\n\n## Block 3: notes — Certification statement and signature of the Registered Professional Land Surveyor who performed the survey.\n\nTHIS SURVEY WAS PERFORMED WITHOUT THE BENEFIT OF A CURRENT\nTITLE COMMITMENT AND THERE MAY BE EASEMENTS, BUILDING LINES,\nCONDITIONS, OR RESTRICTIONS OF RECORD NOT SHOWN OR NOTED\nHEREON.\nDATE OF SURVEY: DECEMBER 27, 2024\nRYAN T. LENZ\nREGISTERED PROFESSIONAL LAND SURVEYOR NO. 7624\nSINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\nTBPELS FIRM No. 10089000\n4150 FREIDRICH LANE, SUITE A-1\nAUSTIN, TEXAS 78744\n(512) 443-1174\n\n## Block 4: notes — List of cities where Bleyl Engineering operates.\n\nAustin Bryan Conroe Houston\n\n## Block 5: notes — Information regarding the coordinate system and bearing basis used for the survey.\n\nBEARING BASIS:\nBEARINGS, DISTANCES AND COORDINATES ARE\nBASED ON THE TEXAS COORDINATE SYSTEM\nOF 1983 (NAD83) CENTRAL ZONE, GRID.\n\n## Block 6: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n\nJOB NUMBER: 20240953\n\n## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n\nLEGEND\n\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n- MAG NAIL SET\n- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n- NAIL FOUND\n- 60D NAIL FOUND\n- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n- IRON PIPE FOUND\n- MAG NAIL FOUND\n- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n- WATER METER\n- WATER VALVE\n- SPRINKLE FOUND\n- WOOD FENCE\n- UTILITY POLE\n- WIRE FENCE\n- LIGHT POLE\n- CRETE FENCE\n- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n- W.L. WATER LINE\n- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n- T.L. TOWN LOT\n- C.I. CURB INLET\n- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n- - CLEAN-OUT\n- - FIRE HYDRANT\n- - AIR CONDITIONER\n- - SIGN POST\n- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- R.P.R.T.C.TX. REAL PROPERTY RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- P.R.T.C.TX. PLAT RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- D.R.T.C.TX. DEED RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- T. TRAFFIC SIGN\n- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n\n## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n\nTREE TABLE\n| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4012 | 12\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4013 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4014 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4015 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4016 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4017 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4019 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4022 | 24\" | PECAN |\n| 4023 | 24\" | M |\n| 4024 | 8\" | ELM |\n| 4025 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4026 | 28\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4027 | 15\" | M |\n| 4028 | 36\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4030 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4031 | 16\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4032 | 18\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4033 | 11\" | ELM |\n| 4034 | 20\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4035 | 16\" | ELM |\n| 4036 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4037 | 11\" | ASH |\n| 4038 | 20\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4040 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4041 | 13\" | ELM |\n| 4042 | 34\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4043 | 15\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4044 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4045 | 20\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4046 | 17\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4047 | 16\" | PINE |\n\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776445241761,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wmvfNNQx75g7YU5EKYuBo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n     4→\n     5→[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    10→\n    11→A detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 4: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n    14→\n    15→**Benchmarks**\n    16→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    17→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    18→\n    19→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    20→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    21→\n    22→## Block 5: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n    23→\n    24→**Tree List**\n    25→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    26→\n    27→**Note**\n    28→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n    29→\n    30→## Block 6: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n    31→\n    32→**Utility Notes**\n    33→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    34→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    35→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n    36→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n    37→\n    38→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    39→\n    40→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    41→\n    42→## Block 7: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n    43→\n    44→See Sht. 19\n    45→for Profile\n    46→\n    47→## Block 11: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n    48→\n    49→**Legal Description**\n    50→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    51→\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"848e4c7a-0ebd-4c8c-8f6e-1da50c4b3f33","uuid":"28df9662-7291-4b74-961a-05141a738cf6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n\n[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\nA detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 5: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n\n**Tree List**\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n**Note**\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n## Block 6: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n\nSee Sht. 19\nfor Profile\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
