{"level":30,"time":1776445243546,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015yf64VADY1ynVWHFDYaGdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have key information:\n\nFrom Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) blocks: \"Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\" are shown on the landscape plan drawing\n\nFrom Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) blocks: \"The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters.\"\n\nSo the electrical plan shows UNDERGROUND lines, but the landscape plan shows OVERHEAD ELECTRIC lines.\n\nThis is critical! The landscape plan shows overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure. This means:\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.6, EL-2.14, and EL-2.15 may be applicable\n- EL-2.7 may be applicable if there's pad-mounted equipment\n- EL-2.8 and EL-2.9 may be applicable if there's underground equipment\n\nBut I need to:\n1. Verify if there are actual overhead lines shown (and what type - distribution or transmission)\n2. Verify if trees are proposed near those lines\n3. Check the plant schedule for species identification and utility compatibility\n\nLet me check the plant schedule/legend blocks for Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations) which likely has the plant schedule.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3333,"cache_read_input_tokens":39865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3333},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e75f7197-0cf3-4f1a-bbad-a48e83eecb6f","uuid":"0b28822b-c817-4174-9f59-37a81dabd84f"}
