{"level":30,"time":1776445244265,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WHWA6sdJUr8RDYmfuTVh4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I found important information:\n\nFrom Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) blocks:\n- In the legend (Block 9), I can see:\n  - \"UTILITY POLE\" - a symbol for utility poles\n  - \"LIGHT POLE\" - a symbol for light poles\n  - \"O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" - a symbol for overhead utility lines\n\nFrom Sheet 9 (Site Plan) blocks:\n- Block 3 notes: \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed.\"\n- Block 7 notes: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\"\n\nSo the legend on Sheet 4 INDICATES that overhead utility lines exist (O.H.U.L.), and from the facts.md I know there are electric easements shown as plat-dedicated.\n\nHowever, I need to look directly at the vision analysis or the drawing blocks to see if there are ACTUAL overhead electric poles/lines shown on the existing conditions survey or site plan. Let me check the vision outputs for these sheets.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5466,"cache_read_input_tokens":44805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5466},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f309802-c1eb-4364-b84a-07fe4c2517f2","uuid":"37bcdebc-0195-41a6-bff6-dcc1c38a276d"}
