{"level":30,"time":1776445253007,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HdSKVLbXQVyrxbVsi2Wiaf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have the plant schedule. The shade trees being proposed are:\n- 2 Live Oak (QUERCUS VIRGINIANA) - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. minimum\n- 10 Cedar Elm (ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA) - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. minimum\n\nAnd from the guide, there are also:\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal)\n\nThe schedule shows \"16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\" which suggests installed height, not mature height. I need to check ECM Appendix F to determine the mature heights of these species.\n\nKey findings so far:\n1. Sheet 31 mentions \"overhead electric (OHE)\" as shown on the landscape plan\n2. Sheet 21 shows underground electric infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, underground lines)\n3. The site has 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm trees proposed (plus other species)\n\nNow I need to use the vision tool to examine:\n1. Whether overhead electric lines are actually shown on Sheet 31\n2. Where trees are located relative to electrical infrastructure\n3. The relationship between the utility lines and the tree locations\n\nBut first, let me check if there's information about ECM Appendix F in the existing vision analysis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3755,"cache_read_input_tokens":44166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3755},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"848e4c7a-0ebd-4c8c-8f6e-1da50c4b3f33","uuid":"e8da0991-3292-4888-b5b8-8b9c01de6a99"}
