{"level":30,"time":1776445269384,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify ALL transformer pad locations on the site. For each transformer pad, please provide:\n\n1. Location description (which building(s) it serves, general position on site)\n2. Specific clearances and distances shown on the plan to:\n   - Nearest building (with building name/number if labeled)\n   - Any fences, gates, or barriers nearby\n   - Sidewalks or pavement\n   - Any pools, recreational areas, or patios\n   - Fire hydrants\n   - Parking areas or drive lanes\n   - Other utilities or equipment pads\n3. Access door orientation (which direction does the access door face?)\n4. Whether the transformer pad appears to be surrounded by fencing or barriers\n5. Any notes about setbacks or clearances written on the plan\n6. Whether the pads appear to be in drainage easements or other restricted areas\n\nProvide exact measurements if shown on the plan, and describe spatial relationships clearly.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" I have identified four (4) distinct locations labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n\n**Important General Note:** This specific plan sheet does **not** provide specific numerical measurements (e.g., \"10 ft\", \"5 ft\") for clearances or distances between the transformer pads and surrounding structures. Spatial relationships described below are based purely on visual proximity as drawn. Furthermore, the plan does **not** indicate access door orientation (typically shown with dashed clearance boxes) for any of the transformer pads.\n\nHere is the detailed breakdown for each identified transformer pad:\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest Corner)\n*   **Location Description:** Located in the northwest corner of the site near the main entrance off Valley View Road.\n*   **Clearances and Distances (Visual):**\n    *   **Nearest building:** Located west of **Bldg. 1**.\n    *   **Fences, gates, or barriers:** None shown around the pad.\n    *   **Sidewalks or pavement:** Located immediately adjacent to a curved sidewalk (labeled nearby as \"Sidewalk Easement\") and the entrance driveway curb.\n    *   **Pools, recreational areas, or patios:** None nearby.\n    *   **Fire hydrants:** None nearby.\n    *   **Parking areas or drive lanes:** Located adjacent to the main entrance drive lane.\n    *   **Other utilities/equipment:** Located near an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** to its south and **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the west wall of Bldg. 1.\n*   **Access door orientation:** Not indicated on the plan.\n*   **Fencing or barriers:** Does not appear to be surrounded by fencing or barriers.\n*   **Notes about setbacks/clearances:** None provided.\n*   **Easements/Restricted areas:** Situated within or immediately adjacent to a hatched area denoted by a line labeled **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"** (document number unclear).\n\n### 2. Transformer Pad 2 (West Side)\n*   **Location Description:** Located on the western edge of the site, directly adjacent to the south side of Bldg. 2.\n*   **Clearances and Distances (Visual):**\n    *   **Nearest building:** Placed immediately against or extremely close to the south wall of **Bldg. 2** (specifically near **Unit 201**).\n    *   **Fences, gates, or barriers:** None shown around the pad.\n    *   **Sidewalks or pavement:** Located adjacent to a sidewalk running north-south along the western property boundary.\n    *   **Pools, recreational areas, or patios:** None nearby.\n    *   **Fire hydrants:** None nearby.\n    *   **Parking areas or drive lanes:** Not near a drive lane.\n    *   **Other utilities/equipment:** Located near an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** and **\"Electrical Meters\