{"level":30,"time":1776445270225,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MQMEFLPdLYaRhLReDuVoN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n     4→\n     5→NORTH\n     6→[North Arrow Symbol]\n     7→SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n     8→0 10 20 50\n     9→\n    10→## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n    11→\n    12→This block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n    13→- Building footprints\n    14→- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n    15→- Sidewalks and pathways\n    16→- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n    17→- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n    18→- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n    19→- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n    20→- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n    21→- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n    22→- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n    23→\n    24→## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n    25→\n    26→NOTE:\n    27→FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    56→3759 VALLEY\n    57→VIEW ROAD,\n    58→AUSTIN,\n    59→TEXAS 78704\n    60→\n    61→## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n    62→\n    63→PROJECT NAME:\n    64→VALLEY VIEW\n    65→TOWNHOMES\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"0e1c8810-66e8-4970-939e-f059e771212b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776445270230,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ND7gJS5p6UX9gQktxJaiR3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    15→* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    16→* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n    17→* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    19→* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n    20→* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n    21→* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n    22→* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    23→* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    26→\n    27→* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    28→  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n    29→  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n    30→\n    31→* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n    32→  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n    33→  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n    34→\n    35→* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n    36→  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n    37→  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n    38→\n    39→* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n    40→  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n    41→  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n    42→\n    43→* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n    44→  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n    45→  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n    46→\n    47→* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n    48→  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n    49→  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n    50→\n    51→* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    52→  Provides surveyor reference points.\n    53→  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n    54→\n    55→* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n    56→  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n    57→  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n    58→\n    59→* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    60→  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n    61→  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baebfa71-225a-4ef1-87a6-157059cbeeb0","uuid":"2c81e5ea-04b5-4536-a2a9-317f2b6096df","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n\nSite plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n\n**Key values**:\n* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n\n* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n\n* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n\n* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n\n* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n\n* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n\n* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n  Provides surveyor reference points.\n  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n\n* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n\n* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
