{"level":30,"time":1776445279545,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WNcqswZiMYQvfCcvGiV5Gr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've got the blocks information:\n\n**Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan)**: Shows overhead electric (OHE) lines, along with water and storm drain lines on the drawing. The landscape blocks don't mention any specific clearance requirements for overhead utilities.\n\n**Sheet 11 (Grading Plan)**: Shows various easements including \"electric and telephone easements\" and lots of infrastructure, but the blocks don't mention any overhead electric lines or clearance details.\n\nNow I need to visually examine these sheets to understand:\n1. Where the overhead electric lines are located\n2. What clearances are maintained from buildings, driveways, trees, etc.\n3. Whether any 48-hour notification notes are present\n4. Whether any profile/section views exist showing vertical clearances\n\nLet me use the vision tool to examine the critical sheets. I'll start with:\n1. Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions) - to see where overhead utilities currently exist\n2. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) - to see overhead electric lines and tree clearances\n3. Sheet 21 (Electrical Design) - to see where new electrical infrastructure is proposed\n\nActually, let me think about what checklist items are most likely to apply based on what I know:\n\nThe grouping includes 47 checklist items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47) covering:\n- Building clearances from overhead lines (EL-1.1, 1.3, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8)\n- Customer facility clearances (EL-1.2, 1.5)\n- Fence clearances (EL-1.9, 1.10, 1.11, 1.12, 1.13)\n- Retaining wall clearances (EL-1.14, 1.15, 1.17)\n- Driveway/parking clearances (EL-1.18, 1.19)\n- Building projection clearances (EL-1.3, 1.16, 1.34)\n\n\n- Tree clearances (EL-1.37), meter locations (EL-1.38), and service-drop clearances (EL-1.28) along with various other utilities and structures.\n\nSince Sheet 31 explicitly shows overhead electric lines, I need to visually inspect it to identify where those lines run, what structures are positioned nearby, whether clearances are dimensioned, and if trees are located close enough to require attention.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3596,"cache_read_input_tokens":62345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3596},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"ad65116c-0bf5-419c-b959-a904cbf50755"}
