{"level":30,"time":1776445282934,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Xce6oRXt3G4RAiRXYVQSKW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important information! The vision tool found:\n\n1. There IS an overhead electric (OHE) line running along the southern boundary (outside the limit of construction)\n2. There ARE proposed trees in close proximity to this OHE line:\n   - Southwest corner: one tree very close to the OHE line\n   - Southeast corner: two trees very close to the OHE line\n3. There are NO visible dimension lines or distance notations showing clearances from trees to the OHE line\n\nThis is potentially a major finding. I need to:\n1. Measure the exact clearance distances from these trees to the overhead electric line using the measure-distance tool\n2. Determine what voltage/type (distribution vs. transmission) the overhead line is\n3. Cross-reference the tree species to check their utility compatibility\n\nLet me first check if there are any notes on Sheet 31 or Sheet 21 that describe the overhead line voltage/type. Let me also look for any site plan (Sheet 9) information about utilities.\n\nBefore I use the measure-distance tool, I need to understand:\n- What voltage is the OHE line (distribution <60kV or transmission ≥60kV)?\n- Are the trees within 15 feet (for distribution) or 50 feet (for transmission) of the overhead conductor?\n\nLet me read the site plan Sheet 9 to see if there's any information about the overhead line.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":48791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_man