{"level":30,"time":1776445283293,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical site plan and identify all transformer pad locations, their dimensions, and their spatial relationships to nearby buildings, structures, property lines, easements, parking areas, and other site features. For each transformer pad visible on the plan:\n\n1. List its location (e.g., \"near Building 1, northeast corner\")\n2. Note its dimensions if shown (e.g., \"5'x5'\")\n3. Measure or estimate its distance from:\n   - Nearest building walls\n   - Any fire lanes or parking areas\n   - Property lines\n   - Any fences or gates\n   - Any visible utility lines or pull boxes\n   - Any access roads or driveways\n\n4. Identify the access door orientation (which direction the access door faces)\n5. Note whether the transformer appears to be in an open area or near any enclosed areas/niches\n6. Check for any bollards, barriers, or protective features shown\n7. Identify any vegetation, trees, shrubs, or landscape features near the transformers\n\nPlease provide specific measurements or distance estimates where possible, and note the scale (1\" = 20') to help determine actual distances.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided electrical site plan (Scale 1\" = 20'), here is a report on the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations and their specific relationships to site features.\n\n**General Observations Applicable to All Transformer Pads:**\n*   **Total Count:** There are exactly five (5) locations explicitly labeled with a leader line pointing to a blue square box reading \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\".\n*   **Dimensions (Point 2):** None of the transformer pads have dimensions (e.g., 5'x5') indicated on the plan. They are represented uniformly by a small blue square containing the letter \"E\".\n*   **Door Orientation (Point 4):** There is no visual indication (such as hinges, handles, or clearance zones) showing the orientation of access doors on any of the transformer pads.\n*   **Protective Features (Point 6):** There are no bollards, barriers, or specific protective enclosures drawn or labeled around any of the transformer pads.\n\nBelow is the specific breakdown for each of the five identified transformer pads:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Northwest Transformer Pad\n*   **Location:** West side of the site, adjacent to **Bldg. 1**, specifically near **Unit 101**.\n*   **Nearest building walls:** The pad symbol is drawn immediately adjacent to (touching) the west-facing exterior wall of Unit 101.\n*   **Fire lanes or parking areas:** It is located directly on the eastern edge of the main paved entrance driveway/access road that curves into the site.\n*   **Property lines:** Visually estimated to be roughly 20-30 feet east of the westernmost property line boundary.\n*   **Fences or gates:** None visible in the immediate vicinity.\n*   **Visible utility lines or pull boxes:** Connected to a solid blue electrical line running north-south. An \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" is located approximately 30-40 feet to the north along this line. A label for \"**Electrical Meters**\" points to the north wall of Bldg 1 nearby.\n*   **Access roads or driveways:** Immediately adjacent to the primary internal access driveway.\n*   **Openness:** Placed against an exterior wall, un-enclosed, next to a paved driveway.\n*   **Vegetation/Landscaping:** There is a large circular dashed outline indicating a tree canopy located immediately to the west/southwest of the pad.\n\n### 2. West Middle Transformer Pad\n*   **Location:** West side of the site, adjacent to **Bldg. 2**, specifically near **Unit 201**.\n*   **Nearest building walls:** The pad symbol is drawn immediately adjacent to (touching) the west-facing exterior wall of Unit 201.\n*   **Fire lanes or parking areas:** It appears to be situated in a pedestrian or side-yard area, set back approximately 15-20 feet east of a dashed line indicating a potential drive or sidewalk easement.\n*   **Property lines:** Visually estimated to be roughly 30-40 feet east of the western outer property line.\n*   **Fences or gates:** None visible in the immediate vicinity.\n*   **Visible utility lines or pull boxes:** Connected to the main solid blue north-south electrical line. A label for \"**Electrical Meters**\" points to the building wall just south of the pad. An \"**Underground Electric Line**\" (dashed blue) connects to the main line further south.\n*   **Access roads or driveways:** Not directly adjacent to a vehicular driveway.\n*   **Openness:** Placed against a flat exterior wall in an open yard area; not enclosed in a niche.\n*   **Vegetation/Landscaping:** A very large circular tree canopy outline is drawn immediately to the west, partially overlapping the space in front of the pad.\n\n### 3. Southwest Transformer Pad\n*   **Location:** Southwest corner of the main building complex, adjacent to **Bldg. 8**, specifically near **Unit 801**.\n*   **Nearest building walls:** The pad symbol is drawn immediately adjacent to (touching) the west-facing exterior wall of Unit 801.\n*   **Fire lanes or parking areas:** It is situated east of an area labeled \"**Sidewalk Easement**\" and near the southern curve of the internal drive/parking area.\n*   **Property lines:** Visually estimated to be roughly 20-30 feet east of the western property line.\n*   **Fences or gates:** None visible nearby.\n*   **Visible utility lines or pull boxes:** Connected to the solid blue electrical line. An \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" is drawn immediately adjacent to the south side of the transformer pad. A label for \"**Electrical Meters**\" points to the south wall of Unit 801.\n*   **Access roads or driveways:** Located near the edge of the internal curving driveway/parking area.\n*   **Openness:** Placed against an exterior wall, un-enclosed.\n*   **Vegetation/Landscaping:** Large circular tree canopy outlines are located to the west and southwest, slightly set back from the pad.\n\n### 4. East Middle Transformer Pad\n*   **Location:** Located on the eastern side of the site, in the pedestrian space/courtyard between **Bldg. 4** (near Unit 404) and **Bldg. 5** (near Unit 504).\n*   **Nearest building walls:** Unlike the western pads, this pad is detached from the buildings. It is located roughly 5-10 feet south of Building 5's south wall and east of Building 4's east wall, situated near a sidewalk corner.\n*   **Fire lanes or parking areas:** Not located near any vehicular areas; situated in an internal courtyard.\n*   **Property lines:** Visually estimated to be roughly 40-50 feet west of the eastern property boundary (near the area labeled \"25' Drainage Easement\").\n*   **Fences or gates:** A faint dashed line labeled \"**Wood Fence**\" runs north-south approximately 20-30 feet to the east.\n*   **Visible utility lines or pull boxes:** Connected to a solid blue line network. An \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" is located roughly 5-10 feet to the west. Labels for \"**Electrical Meters**\" point to the nearby building walls.\n*   **Access roads or driveways:** Internal pedestrian pathway area only.\n*   **Openness:** Located in an open, un-enclosed courtyard space between building masses.\n*   **Vegetation/Landscaping:** Set within a courtyard area, but no major tree canopy circles immediately overlap the pad itself.\n\n### 5. Southeast Transformer Pad\n*   **Location:** Located in the southeastern section of the site, in the pedestrian space between **Bldg. 7** (near Unit 703/704) and **Bldg. 6** (near Unit 602/603).\n*   **Nearest building walls:** Detached from the buildings, similar to Pad #4. It is located approximately 5-10 feet south of Building 6's south wall and east of Building 7's east wall.\n*   **Fire lanes or parking areas:** Not located near vehicular areas.\n*   **Property lines:** Visually estimated to be roughly 30-40 feet west of the eastern property boundary.\n*   **Fences or gates:** The line labeled \"**Wood Fence**\" is located approximately 15-25 feet to the east.\n*   **Visible utility lines or pull boxes:** Connected to the solid blue electrical line. An \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" is located approximately 10 feet to the west. A red fire line and a \"**FH**\" (Fire Hydrant) symbol are located a short distance to the southeast.\n*   **Access roads or driveways:** Internal pedestrian pathway area only.\n*   **Openness:** Located in an open, un-enclosed area between buildings.\n*   **Vegetation/Landscaping:** A circular tree canopy outline is drawn just to the east of the pad location.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1552,"outputTokens":1759,"totalTokens":6341,"reasoningTokens":3030},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back 