{"level":30,"time":1776445417322,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan for proposed trees and their locations relative to overhead electric (OHE) utility lines. Identify which trees are closest to the overhead electric lines shown on the plan. Note their approximate distances from the OHE lines and their locations (e.g., near which buildings or areas). Are any trees shown within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric lines? What tree symbols/types are used for trees near utilities (e.g., SY for street yard, PL for parking lot, M for mitigation)?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding proposed trees and their proximity to the overhead electric lines:\n\n**Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines:**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a line style marked with \"---OHE---\" running horizontally along the bottom edge of the site plan, parallel to the property boundary/street line.\n\n**Trees Closest to Overhead Electric Lines:**\nUsing the graphic scale provided at the bottom right of the page (1\" = 20'-0\", with a 10-foot increment marker), several trees are plotted in close proximity to the OHE line along the bottom boundary.\n\n1.  **Bottom Left Area:**\n    *   **Location:** Near the bottom left corner of the site, adjacent to the proposed paving/entrance drive.\n    *   **Distance:** The center crosshair of this tree is plotted almost directly on top of the line indicating the OHE. It is well within the 10-15 foot range; the trunk appears to be **0 to 5 feet** from the OHE line.\n    *   **Tree Symbol/Type:** This tree is labeled with an \"**M**\". According to the Key Notes on the right side of the plan, \"M\" stands for \"MITIGATION TREE\".\n\n2.  **Bottom Right Area:**\n    *   **Location:** A cluster of three trees is shown near the bottom right corner of the site, south of the building structure.\n    *   **Distance:**\n        *   The leftmost large tree in this cluster has its center crosshair plotted very close to the OHE line. Visually comparing it to the 10-foot scale bar, the center appears to be approximately **10 feet** from the OHE line.\n        *   The rightmost smaller tree in this cluster also appears to have its center crosshair approximately **10 feet** from the OHE line.\n        *   The middle large tree in this cluster is plotted slightly further north, approximately 15 to 20 feet from the OHE line.\n    *   **Tree Symbol/Type:**\n        *   The two larger trees in this cluster are labeled with both \"**M**\" and \"**SY**\". According to the Key Notes, \"M\" is \"MITIGATION TREE\" and \"SY\" is \"STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\".\n        *   The smaller tree on the far right is labeled \"**M**\" (\"MITIGATION TREE\").\n\n**Summary Answer:**\nYes, there are trees shown within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric lines. Specifically, one mitigation tree (\"M\") on the bottom left is plotted almost directly beneath the OHE line, and at least two trees (labeled \"M\" and \"SY/M\") in the bottom right corner are plotted approximately 10 feet away from the OHE line. The symbols used for these nearby trees are \"M\" (Mitigation Tree) and \"SY\" (Street Yard Tree).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1419,"outputTokens":659,"totalTokens":3501,"reasoningTokens":1423},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan for proposed trees and their locations relative to overhead electric (OHE) utility lines. Identify which trees are closest to the overhead electric lines shown on the plan. Note their approximate distances from the OHE lines and their locations (e.g., near which buildings or areas). Are any trees shown within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric lines? What tree symbols/types are used for trees near utilities (e.g., SY for street yard, PL for parking lot, M for mitigation)?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-pyFzq6V5KrqWVbrIuYMV9s6l","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-st