50'57\"W 414.24'`). It is located mostly inside the property boundary, situated to the south of the central existing structure.\n\n**2) All locations marked as \"ELECTRIC EASEMENT\" (dimensions and locations):**\n*   **Northern Property Area:** Located parallel to and just inside the northern property line (`S63°03'28\"E 419.86'`), there is a dashed rectangular area labeled:\n    *   `10' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n    *   `VOL. 8303, PG. 78`\n    *   `P.R.T.C.TX`\n*   **Southern Property Area:** Located parallel to and just inside the southern property line (`N63°50'57\"W 414.24'`), roughly midway along the line, there is a dashed rectangular area labeled:\n    *   `5' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n    *   `VOL. 8303, PG. 78`\n    *   `P.R.T.C.TX`\n*   **Southeast Property Area:** Located near the southeast corner/eastern boundary area, there is a dashed line indicating an area labeled:\n    *   `5' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n    *   `VOL. 848, PG. 888`\n    *   `D.R.T.C.TX`\n\n**3) Power poles shown on adjacent Valley View Road or on the property itself:**\n*   *Based on the \"U.P.\" symbol identified in the legend:*\n    *   **Northwest Area:** There is a \"U.P.\" symbol located near the northwest corner of the property boundary, adjacent to Valley View Road.\n    *   **Southwest Area:** There is a \"U.P.\" symbol located near the southwest corner of the property boundary, adjacent to Valley View Road.\n    *   **Northeast Area:** There is a \"U.P.\" symbol located near the eastern end of the northern property line (near a point marked `1.38' SOUTH OF LINE`).\n*   These poles appear to serve as anchor or turning points for the \"- OH -\" lines that traverse the perimeter of the property.\n\n**4) The relationship of these utility features to existing trees and structures:**\n*   **Relationship to Structure:** The overhead utility lines (\"- OH -\") form a perimeter buffer on three sides of the primary central structure (\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"). They run along the north, west, and south edges of t