{"level":30,"time":1776445417325,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bSE72LkLr9HZvqif4UwuU","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding proposed trees and their proximity to the overhead electric lines:\n\n**Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines:**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a line style marked with \"---OHE---\" running horizontally along the bottom edge of the site plan, parallel to the property boundary/street line.\n\n**Trees Closest to Overhead Electric Lines:**\nUsing the graphic scale provided at the bottom right of the page (1\" = 20'-0\", with a 10-foot increment marker), several trees are plotted in close proximity to the OHE line along the bottom boundary.\n\n1.  **Bottom Left Area:**\n    *   **Location:** Near the bottom left corner of the site, adjacent to the proposed paving/entrance drive.\n    *   **Distance:** The center crosshair of this tree is plotted almost directly on top of the line indicating the OHE. It is well within the 10-15 foot range; the trunk appears to be **0 to 5 feet** from the OHE line.\n    *   **Tree Symbol/Type:** This tree is labeled with an \"**M**\". According to the Key Notes on the right side of the plan, \"M\" stands for \"MITIGATION TREE\".\n\n2.  **Bottom Right Area:**\n    *   **Location:** A cluster of three trees is shown near the bottom right corner of the site, south of the building structure.\n    *   **Distance:**\n        *   The leftmost large tree in this cluster has its center crosshair plotted very close to the OHE line. Visually comparing it to the 10-foot scale bar, the center appears to be approximately **10 feet** from the OHE line.\n        *   The rightmost smaller tree in this cluster also appears to have its center crosshair approximately **10 feet** from the OHE line.\n        *   The middle large tree in this cluster is plotted slightly further north, approximately 15 to 20 feet from the OHE line.\n    *   **Tree Symbol/Type:**\n        *   The two larger trees in this cluster are labeled with both \"**M**\" and \"**SY**\". According to the Key Notes, \"M\" is \"MITIGATION TREE\" and \"SY\" is \"STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\".\n        *   The smaller tree on the far right is labeled \"**M**\" (\"MITIGATION TREE\").\n\n**Summary Answer:**\nYes, there are trees shown within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric lines. Specifically, one mitigation tree (\"M\") on the bottom left is plotted almost directly beneath the OHE line, and at least two trees (labeled \"M\" and \"SY/M\") in the bottom right corner are plotted approximately 10 feet away from the OHE line. The symbols used for these nearby trees are \"M\" (Mitigation Tree) and \"SY\" (Street Yard Tree)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97c9d1ef-3ef8-4a72-b129-cbdede465e25","uuid":"fdc7dc7a-dac7-453d-a3cc-0a27841dbef2","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding proposed trees and their proximity to the overhead electric lines:\n\n**Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines:**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a line style marked with \"---OHE---\" running horizontally along the bottom edge of the site plan, parallel to the property boundary/street line.\n\n**Trees Closest to Overhead Electric Lines:**\nUsing the graphic scale provided at the bottom right of the page (1\" = 20'-0\", with a 10-foot increment marker), several trees are plotted in close proximity to the OHE line along the bottom boundary.\n\n1.  **Bottom Left Area:**\n    *   **Location:** Near the bottom left corner of the site, adjacent to the proposed paving/entrance drive.\n    *   **Di