{"level":30,"time":1776445417325,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"This sheet is the Existing Conditions Survey for the Valley View Townhomes project. The legend indicates symbols for utility poles, light poles, and overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.). Please examine the drawing and identify:\n\n1. Whether any utility poles are shown on the property (these would appear as small circles or symbols marked with \"UTILITY POLE\" per the legend)\n2. Whether any overhead utility lines are shown (these would appear as lines overhead, connecting poles, marked with \"O.H.U.L.\" per the legend)\n3. The location and spacing of any utility poles relative to the property boundaries\n4. Whether the poles appear to be distribution poles or transmission towers\n5. Any electrical infrastructure visible on the existing site\n\nFocus on documenting what EXISTS today, not what is proposed.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey\" sheet, here are the findings regarding your specific questions about utility infrastructure:\n\n**1. Whether any utility poles are shown on the property**\nYes, utility poles are present. According to the legend, they are identified by a circular symbol with an \"X\" inside. \n*   There are five (5) utility poles clearly identifiable on or immediately adjacent to the surveyed area.\n*   Most appear to be situated just outside the property boundary lines in the adjacent right-of-way or easement areas.\n\n**2. Whether any overhead utility lines are shown**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown. According to the legend, these are indicated by a line with \"- OH -\" inserted intermittently.\n*   An overhead utility line runs continuously along the western edge of the site, adjacent to \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\".\n*   An overhead utility line runs along the eastern boundary of the site.\n*   There is a service drop overhead utility line branching off from the middle pole on Valley View Road and connecting directly to the existing residential structure on the property.\n\n**3. The location and spacing of any utility poles relative to the property boundaries**\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road):** Three (3) utility poles are located just outside the western property line, positioned along the road's right-of-way. \n    *   One is located near the northernmost corner of the Valley View Road frontage (adjacent to the property line labeled \"N28°04'28\\\"E 93.28'\"). This pole also has a labeled \"GUY WIRE\".\n    *   One is located roughly midway along the property frontage on Valley View Road.\n    *   One is located near the southernmost corner of the Valley View Road frontage.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Two (2) utility poles are located along the eastern edge of the site, seemingly associated with the overhead line running near the eastern property line (labeled \"S27°19'28\\\"W 146.15'\").\n    *   One is situated near the northeastern corner.\n    *   One is situated near the southeastern corner.\n*   *(Note: Exact spacing in feet cannot be definitively stated without physically measuring against the provided 1\"=20' graphic scale, but they are distributed along the full lengths of the eastern and western boundaries).*\n\n**4. Whether the poles appear to be distribution poles or transmission towers**\nBased on the standard symbology used (a simple circle with an \"X\"), the \"UTILITY POLE\" label, and the context of a residential site where these poles directly feed a local house meter via a service drop, these appear to be standard local **distribution poles**. There is no visual evidence or specialized symbology to suggest large-scale transmission towers.\n\n**5. Any electrical infrastructure visible on the existing site**\n*   **Electric Meter:** An electric meter is visible on the existing building. Following the overhead service line from Valley View Road to the house, it terminates at a small square symbol containing an \"E\". The legend confirms this symbol represents an \"ELECTRIC METER/BOX\". It is located on the west-facing exterior wall of the main structure.\n*   **Easements:** While not physical infrastructure, there are specifically designated existing electrical easements shown on the eastern portion of the property, labeled \"5' ELEC. EASEMENT\" and \"10' ELEC. EASEMENT\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1480,"outputTokens":728,"totalTokens":4804,"reasoningTokens":2596},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant i