ng the southern property boundary."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"c580a40f-35fa-487c-9d9b-8f33573f7f52","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey\" (Sheet 4), here are the findings regarding your specific questions about overhead utilities:\n\n**1) Locations marked as \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" (O.H.U.L.) or \"UTILITY POLE\" relative to boundaries and structures:**\n*   *Note: The legend indicates that the symbol \"- OH -\" represents \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" and \"U.P.\" represents \"UTILITY POLE\".*\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road):** An \"- OH -\" line runs roughly parallel to the western property boundary (along Valley View Road), located just inside the property line. It runs north-south, positioned to the west of the central existing structure (\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\").\n*   **Northern Boundary:** An \"- OH -\" line runs eastward from the Valley View Road area, roughly parallel to the northern property line (`S63°03'28\"E 419.86'`). It is located inside the property line, situated to the north of the central existing structure.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** An \"- OH -\" line runs southeastward from the Valley View Road area, roughly parallel to the southern property line (`N63°50'57\"W 414.24'`). It is located mostly inside the property boundary, situated to the south of the central existing structure.\n\n**2) All locations marked as \"ELECTRIC EASEMENT\" (dimensions and locations):**\n*   **Northern Property Area:** Located parallel to and just inside the northern property line (`S63°03'28\"E 419.86'`), there is a dashed rectangular area labeled:\n    *   `10' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n    *   `VOL. 8303, PG. 78`\n    *   `P.R.T.C.TX`\n*   **Southern Property Area:** Located parallel to and just inside the southern property line (`N63°50'57\"W 414.24'`), roughly midway along the line, there is a dashed rectangular area labeled:\n