ols (likely existing trees given their irregular, overlapping canopies), some with labels that are difficult to read perfectly but appear to contain \"**SYM**\".\n*   There are smaller, distinct circles with crosshairs indicating proposed trees. Labels visible in this general western area include \"**M**\" (MITIGATION TREE), \"**ST**\" (STREET YARD TREE), and \"**P**\" (PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE). \n*   There are no electrical utility boxes labeled in this area.\n\n**East Side / Courtyard Areas:**\n*   The far eastern section prominently features two large, hatched rectangular structures labeled \"**SEDIMENTATION BASIN**\" and \"**FILTRATION BASIN**\".\n*   The spaces between the building wings (courtyards) primarily show paving patterns and lines labeled \"**- SD -**\" (Storm Drain).\n*   Vegetation in the eastern and courtyard areas includes areas labeled \"**H-7**\" (SOD) and trees labeled \"**PL**\" (PARKING LOT TREE) and \"**M**\" (MITIGATION TREE).\n*   There are no electrical utility boxes or transformer pads labeled in these courtyard or eastern zones.\n\n**Addressing your specific points based strictly on the provided document:**\n\n1.  **Identify all trees and shrubs within 15 feet:** Cannot be determined, as transformer locations are not identified on this sheet.\n2.  **Note the species or type labels:** Cannot be determined relative to transformers. The general tree types defined in the KEY NOTES are ST, PL, P, and M.\n3.  **Measure or estimate distances:** Cannot be determined.\n4.  **Check for root barriers or special clearances:** There are **no** notes, symbols, or callouts indicating root barriers or special electrical vegetation clearances anywhere on this page. \n5.  **Identify existing vs. proposed:** Cannot be evaluated relative to transformers. \n6.  **Landscape details or callouts related to transformers:** There are no callouts or details on this sheet mentioning transformers or electrical equipment. The only utility explicitly labeled is a l