{"level":30,"time":1776445444413,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and identify: 1) All locations of \"Overhead Electric\" (OHE) lines - trace their routing across the property and describe their path relative to buildings, driveways, and parking areas; 2) Any trees shown in proximity to overhead electric lines - identify which trees are within 10 feet horizontal distance of the lines; 3) Whether any clearance dimensions are labeled for overhead lines; 4) Any building features, canopies, or structures that appear to be under or near the overhead lines. Use compass directions and distances if visible on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (noted as Sheet 28 of 35 in the bottom right corner, rather than Sheet 31), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Locations and Routing of \"Overhead Electric\" (OHE) Lines:**\n*   There is a single utility line explicitly labeled **\"-OHE-\"** running along the entire **southern** boundary of the site plan shown. \n*   **Routing:** It enters the viewable area from the southwest corner and runs straight east across the bottom edge of the drawing to the southeast corner.\n*   **Relative Path:** The OHE line is located south of all proposed buildings. It runs parallel to, and south of, the southern surface parking spaces, drive aisle, and a proposed sidewalk. It appears to be located within or immediately adjacent to the southern landscape setback/right-of-way. \n\n**2) Trees in Proximity to Overhead Electric Lines:**\n*   There is a row of several trees planted or preserved along the southern boundary line that are in close proximity to the -OHE- line.\n*   Visually applying the provided scale (1\" = 20'-0\"), several tree trunks 