{"level":30,"time":1776445447189,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y2dTBhMD36o6mFCcGHaU9j","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    15→* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    16→* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n    17→* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    19→* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n    20→* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n    21→* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n    22→* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    23→* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    26→\n    27→* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    28→  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n    29→  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n    30→\n    31→* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n    32→  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n    33→  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n    34→\n    35→* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n    36→  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n    37→  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n    38→\n    39→* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n    40→  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n    41→  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n    42→\n    43→* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n    44→  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n    45→  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n    46→\n    47→* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n    48→  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n    49→  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n    50→\n    51→* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    52→  Provides surveyor reference points.\n    53→  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n    54→\n    55→* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n    56→  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n    57→  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n    58→\n    59→* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    60→  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n    61→  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44f53564-a2c6-473b-bd29-a0ef36023cf2","uuid":"647349a2-f0d4-486c-aeea-e3b22b2b440d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n\nSite plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n\n**Key values**:\n* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n\n* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n\n* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n\n* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n\n* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n\n* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n\n* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n  Provides surveyor reference points.\n  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n\n* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n\n* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776445447923,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"This sheet is the Site Plan (proposed layout) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Please examine the drawing to identify:\n\n1. Whether any overhead electric poles, lines, or conductors are shown on or adjacent to the site\n2. The location of any existing utility poles relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, and parking areas\n3. Whether any overhead utility lines cross over or are adjacent to proposed structures\n4. Any notes or callouts regarding utility clearances or overhead line conflicts\n5. Whether the plan shows existing versus proposed utility infrastructure\n\nFocus on identifying any overhead electric infrastructure that impacts the proposed development.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes, here is the information regarding overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n**1. Whether any overhead electric poles, lines, or conductors are shown on or adjacent to the site**\nYes, overhead utility lines and poles are shown adjacent to and along the perimeter of the site. They are explicitly denoted by lines labeled with \"-- OHE --\" (Overhead Electric).\n*   An \"-- OHE --\" line runs north-south along the entire western boundary of the site (adjacent to the street frontage).\n*   An \"-- OHE --\" line runs east-west along the southern boundary line.\n\n**2. The location of any existing utility poles relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, and parking areas**\nUtility poles are located along the perimeter of the site, primarily along the overhead line routes:\n*   **Northwest Corner:** An \"AT&T Post\" is called out near an existing water manhole, situated north of the proposed northern \"Construct Type II Driveway\" and northwest of Building 1.\n*   **Western Boundary:** Poles are indicated along the \"-- OHE --\" line that parallels the western property boundary. These poles are located in the Right-of-Way/easement area, forward of the building setback line. They do not sit inside the proposed driveways or parking areas but the overhead lines between them cross over the two proposed driveway entrances.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Poles are indicated along the \"-- OHE --\" line on the southern edge of the property. These are located south of the proposed drive aisle, parking spaces, and the proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall,\" remaining well clear of the proposed footprints for Buildings 6, 7, and 8. \n\n**3. Whether any overhead utility lines cross over or are adjacent to proposed structures**\n*   **Adjacent to structures:** The \"-- OHE --\" lines run strictly along the western and southern perimeter boundaries. They are adjacent to the site but are set back from the primary proposed structures (Buildings 1 through 8). \n*   **Crossing over structures:** The overhead lines do not appear to cross directly *over* any of the proposed residential buildings. However, the western \"-- OHE --\" line crosses directly over the two newly proposed entrances (\"Construct Type II Driveway\"). The southern \"-- OHE --\" line runs immediately adjacent to (and potentially over portions of) the proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" that runs along the southern perimeter.\n\n**4. Any notes or callouts regarding utility clearances or overhead line conflicts**\nThere are no explicit notes or warning callouts visible on this sheet regarding overhead line clearance requirements (e.g., OSHA clearance zones) or specific overhead conflicts. The \"Site Plan Release Notes\" mention water/wastewater service and right-of-way excavation, but do not contain safety or clearance notes pertaining to the overhead electric lines. \n\n**5. Whether the plan shows existing versus proposed utility infrastructure**\nThe plan distinguishes between existing perimeter infrastructure and proposed internal infrastructure:\n*   **Existing:** The \"-- OHE --\" lines and utility poles (like the \"AT&T Post\") are shown as existing infrastructure running along the property's exterior easements/Right-of-Way. \n*   **Proposed:** The plan shows proposed \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" locations (e.g., one near Building 1 and another near Building 8). This indicates the proposed method of routing power from the existing overhead lines down to proposed underground feeds for the new buildings. Other proposed utilities are also marked distinctly, such as the \"Wastewater Service Connection\" pointing to an existing line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1436,"outputTokens":758,"totalTokens":4878,"reasoningTokens":2684},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This sheet is the Site Plan (proposed layout) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Please examine the drawing to identify:\n\n1. Whether any overhead electric poles, lines, or conductors are shown on or adjacent to the site\n2. The location of any existing utility poles relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, and parking areas\n3. Whether any overhead utility lines cross over or are adjacent to proposed structures\n4. Any notes or callouts regarding utility clearances or overhead line conflicts\n5. Whether the plan shows existing versus proposed utility infrastructure\n\nFocus on identifying any overhead electric infrastructure that impacts the proposed development."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-9EKV4Gt4H1zxoDBP1ParWVVQ","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 17 Apr 2026 17:04:07 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::kp76z-1776445417863-4d7a4346649b"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes, here is the information regarding overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n**1. Whether any overhead electric poles, lines, or conductors are shown on or adjacent to the site**\nYes, overhead utility lines and poles are shown adjacent to and along the perimeter of the site. They are explicitly denoted by lines labeled with \"-- OHE --\" (Overhead Electric).\n*   An \"-- OHE --\" line runs north-south along the entire western boundary of the site (adjacent to the street frontage).\n*   An \"-- OHE --\" line runs east-west along the southern boundary line.\n\n**2. The location of any existing utility poles relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, and parking areas**\nUtility poles are located along the perimeter of the site, primarily along the overhead line routes:\n*   **Northwest Corner:** An \"AT&T Post\" is called out near an existing water manhole, situated north of the proposed northern \"Construct Type II Driveway\" and northwest of Building 1.\n*   **Western Boundary:** Poles are indicated along the \"-- OHE --\" line that parallels the western property boundary. These poles are located in the Right-of-Way/easement area, forward of the building setback line. They do not sit inside the proposed driveways or parking areas but the overhead lines between them cross over the two proposed driveway entrances.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Poles are indicated along the \"-- OHE --\" line on the southern edge of the property. These are located south of the proposed drive aisle, parking spaces, and the proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall,\" remaining well clear of the proposed footprints for Buildings 6, 7, and 8. \n\n**3. Whether any overhead utility lines cross over or are adjacent to proposed structures**\n*   **Adjacent to structures:** The \"-- OHE --\" lines run strictly along the western and southern perimeter boundaries. They are adjacent to the site but are set back from the primary proposed structures (Buildings 1 through 8). \n*   **Crossing over structures:** The overhead lines do not appear to cross directly *over* any of the proposed residential buildings. However, the western \"-- OHE --\" line crosses directly over the two newly proposed entrances (\"Construct Type II Driveway\"). The southern \"-- OHE --\" line runs immediately adjacent to (and potentially over portions of) the proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" that runs along the southern perimeter.\n\n**4. Any notes or callouts regarding utility clearances or overhead line conflicts**\nThere are no explicit notes or warning callouts visible on this sheet regarding overhead line clearance requirements (e.g., OSHA clearance zones) or specific overhead conflicts. The \"Site Plan Release Notes\" mention water/wastewater service and right-of-way excavation, but do not contain safety or clearance notes pertaining to the overhead electric lines. \n\n**5. Whether the plan shows existing versus proposed utility infrastructure**\nThe plan distinguishes between existing perimeter infrastructure and proposed internal infrastructure:\n*   **Existing:** The \"-- OHE --\" lines and utility poles (like the \"AT&T Post\") are shown as existing infrastructure running along the property's exterior easements/Right-of-Way. \n*   **Proposed:** The plan shows proposed \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" locations (e.g., one near Building 1 and another near Building 8). This indicates the proposed method of routing power from the existing overhead lines down to proposed underground feeds for the new buildings. Other proposed utilities are also marked distinctly, such as the \"Wastewater Service Connection\" pointing to an existing line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1436,"outputTokens":758,"totalTokens":4878,"reasoningTokens":2684},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptF