Oak species are large trees that typically reach 40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F. Plant schedule shows only minimum container heights at planting (16' HT minimum) but does not state mature heights. Large trees are not differentiated from small trees on the landscape plan, preventing verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities required for large tree species."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"Three proposed trees are located in close proximity to the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Clearance dimensions are not provided on plans, so it cannot be determined whether trees are within prohibited zones (less than 15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees or less than 25 feet for large trees from distribution line). No Austin Energy written approval letter is attached to or referenced on the plans authorizing any trees within restricted clearance zones."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1841,"cache_read_input_tokens":70187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1841},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60b9cdbc-bfc6-4085-b89d-09c184480485","uuid":"400b5d03-ce6f-449a-8717-33ae9fb66bc7"}
