{"level":30,"time":1776445700306,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the mitigation trees labeled \"M\" along the southern boundary near the \"-OHE-\" (Overhead Electric) line. Please identify: 1) How many \"M\" trees are shown within 10 feet of the OHE line; 2) For each M tree near the OHE line, estimate its distance from the line (in feet if possible using the 1\"=20' scale); 3) Provide the tree species if labeled; 4) Identify any other new trees (labeled \"SY\", \"PL\", or \"P\") near the overhead line. Use the scale bar provided to estimate distances. Note any trees whose drawn canopy circles appear to cross or overlap the OHE line.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28), here are the findings regarding the trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line:\n\n**1) Number of \"M\" trees within 10 feet of the OHE line:**\nThere is exactly **one (1)** tree labeled \"M\" located along the southern boundary near the dashed line labeled \"-OHE-\".\n\n**2) Estimated distance from the line:**\nLocating the single \"M\" tree in the southeast area of the plan (bottom right quadrant, just north of the southern property line), I used the graphical scale bar provided in the bottom right corner (\"0 10 20 50\"). The visual distance from the center cross mark (trunk location) of the \"M\" tree down to the dashed \"-OHE-\" line appears to be roughly half the length of the 0-10 scale segment. Therefore, the estimated distance is approximately **5 feet**.\n\n**3) Tree species:**\nThe specific tree species is **not labeled** on this sheet. The tree is only designated with the letter \"M\", which corresponds to the definition in the KEY NOTES (bottom right): \"M - MITIGATION TREE\". There is no plant schedule or leader line indicati