{"level":30,"time":1776445700307,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This is the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) showing proposed trees and plantings. The plan shows overhead electric lines (OHE) marked on it. Please examine the plan and identify:\n\n1. The locations of the overhead electric lines (OHE) on the landscape plan\n2. All proposed trees shown on the plan (marked with symbols and indicated as SY=street yard, PL=parking lot, P=buffer point, M=mitigation)\n3. Whether any proposed trees are located within 10 feet of the overhead electric distribution lines (the requirement is that trees planted within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible list in ECM Appendix F, generally trees with mature height ≤20 feet)\n4. Whether any trees are proposed on the western boundary (Valley View Road) near the overhead lines\n5. Whether any trees are proposed on the eastern boundary near the overhead lines\n6. Tree species if visible or notated on the plan\n\nThis information is needed to verify compliance with overhead electric tree clearance requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information requested regarding overhead electric lines and proposed trees:\n\n**1. Locations of the overhead electric lines (OHE) on the landscape plan:**\nAn overhead electric line is explicitly marked with the line type label \"**---OHE---**\" running horizontally along the entire bottom property boundary (which corresponds to the Southern boundary, based on the North arrow pointing to the top of the page). \n\n**2. Proposed trees shown on the plan:**\nNumerous proposed trees are drawn throughout the site, indicated by circles with center marks. They are tagged with the following classifications, which are defined in the \"KEY NOTES\" section at the top right:\n*   **SY** - \"STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **PL** - \"PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **P** - \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   **M** - \"MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**3. Trees located within 10 feet of overhead electric distribution lines:**\n**Yes.** There is a row of proposed trees (primarily labeled with \"**M**\") planted along the bottom (Southern) boundary. The \"**---OHE---**\" line passes directly through the drawn canopies of at least five of these trees. Based on the provided scale (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the center points (trunks) of these trees appear to be situated well within 10 lateral feet of the marked OHE line, with some appearing almost directly underneath it.\n\n**4. Trees proposed on the western boundary (Valley View Road) near overhead lines:**\n*   **Trees Proposed:** Yes. There are several large proposed trees along the western boundary (Valley View Road) within the shaded area designated as \"H-2\" (STREET YARD). These are primarily labeled with \"**SY/M**\".\n*   **Near Overhead Lines:** There are **no overhead electric lines explicitly labeled** (such as \"OHE\") running along this western boundary on this specific sheet. Various other utility and boundary lines are marked (e.g., \"---LOC---\", \"---SD---\"), but OHE is not indicated here.\n\n**5. Trees proposed on the eastern boundary near overhead lines:**\n*   **Trees Proposed:** Yes. There is a row of proposed trees running along the eastern boundary, generally labeled with \"**M**\". \n*   **Near Overhead Lines:** Similar to the western boundary, there are **no overhead electric lines explicitly labeled** along the eastern boundary on this sheet. The lines shown are limits of construction (\"---LOC---\") and a wooden privacy fence (\"---x---\").\n\n**6. Tree species visible or notated on the plan:**\nSpecific botanical or common tree species are **not visible or notated** on this specific plan sheet. The trees are only identified by their functional classifications (SY, PL, P, M) as detailed in the Key Notes. There is no plant schedule or legend providing species names on this page.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1528,"outputTokens":675,"totalTokens":4920,"reasoningTokens":2717},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) showing proposed trees and plantings. The plan shows overhead electric lines (OHE) marked on it. Please examine the plan and identify:\n\n1. The locations of the overhead electric lines (OHE) on the landscape plan\n2. All proposed trees shown on the plan (marked with symbols and indicated as SY=street yard, PL=parking lot, P=buffer point, M=mitigation)\n3. Whether any proposed trees are located within 10 feet of the overhead electric distribution lines (the requirement is that trees planted within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible list in ECM Appendix F, generally trees with mature height ≤20 feet)\n4. Whether any trees are proposed on the western boundary (Valley View Road) near the overhead lines\n5. Whether any trees are proposed on the eastern boundary near the overhead lines\n6. Tree species if visible or notated on the plan\n\nThis information is needed to verify compliance with overhead electric tree clearance requirements."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-ABAZ8ViaROuUPsYv7LwCsnae","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 17 Apr 2026 17:06:47 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::jszxf-1776445579087-0f4ff5bae00e"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","tex