{"level":30,"time":1776445700307,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please identify and describe:\n1. The location of all proposed trees and shrubs on this landscape plan\n2. The species of trees proposed (check for utility-compatible species designation)\n3. The size/maturity of trees proposed (caliper size if shown)\n4. The proximity of trees and shrubs to the four transformer pad locations noted on Sheet 21 (one near Bldg 1, one in central courtyard, one near Bldg 8/SW area, one in south-central area near Bldg 4/7)\n5. Any planting details, spacing, or protective barriers around trees\n6. Any notes about shrubs or low-lying vegetation and their clearances\n7. Root barrier details if shown\nThis will help verify compliance with tree and shrub clearance requirements for transformer pads.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 28 (LANDSCAPE PLAN) of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, here is the information requested. \n\n**CRITICAL NOTE:** This analysis is strictly limited to the visual evidence present on Sheet 28. Information such as specific building numbers, transformer pad labels, detailed plant schedules, and planting detail sections are not present on this specific page.\n\n### 1. Location of all proposed trees and shrubs\n*   **Trees:** Proposed trees are represented by circle symbols (some with internal crosses, dots, or simple outlines). They are distributed extensively throughout the site:\n    *   Along the western edge within the grey-shaded street/parking yard area.\n    *   Within internal courtyards located between the unshaded building footprints.\n    *   Along the northern, eastern, and southern property perimeters.\n    *   Along the southern perimeter, trees are planted near a line denoted as \"- OHE -\" (Overhead Electric).\n*   **Shrubs:** There are no distinct symbols or hatched areas explicitly labeled as individual shrubs on this plan. The plan uses general shading and Key Notes to indicate landscape areas (e.g., \"H-3 STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\" and \"H-4 PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\"), but does not denote specific shrub locations.\n\n### 2. Species of trees proposed\n*   Specific tree species (botanical or common names) and \"utility-compatible\" designations are **not identified** on this sheet. There is no plant schedule or species list provided here.\n*   Trees are identified by functional classifications using abbreviations found below the KEY NOTES section.\n\n### 3. Size/maturity of trees proposed\nSpecific individual caliper sizes are not listed next to each tree. However, minimum caliper sizes are provided in the definitions below the KEY NOTES. They are transcribed exactly as follows:\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\" (No size specified in this note)\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\" (No size specified in this note)\n\n### 4. Proximity of trees/shrubs to transformer pads\n*   **Unable to verify specific locations:** Building numbers (e.g., Bldg 1, Bldg 8) and explicitly labeled transformer pads (as referenced from Sheet 21) are **not present** on this drawing.\n*   **General Observation:** There are several small, unlabeled rectangular outlines (some with crossed lines indicating mechanical/electrical equipment) located near building edges and property lines. Throughout the plan, tree symbols are shown planted in relatively close proximity to the building footprints and internal courtyard walls.\n*   Along the southern property boundary, tree symbols (labeled \"M\") are shown planted directly adjacent to, or directly underneath, a dashed line labeled \"- OHE -\" (Overhead Electric).\n\n### 5. Planting details, spacing, or protective barriers\n*   **Planting Details/Barriers:** There are no section drawings, detail callouts, or symbols indicating planting pit construction, tree staking, or protective barriers/fencing around trees on this sheet.\n*   **Spacing:** Exact spacing measurements between trees are not dimensioned on this plan, though they are visually represented at scale.\n*   **Relevant Notes:** The \"NOTE:\" section in the top middle provides requirements for planting areas in parking lots, transcribed exactly:\n    *   \"FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\"\n\n### 6. Notes about shrubs or low-lying vegetation and clearances\n*   There are **no notes** on this sheet regarding specific shrub types, sizes, or required clearance distances from utilities or structures for low-lying vegetation.\n\n### 7. Root barrier details\n*   There are **no** root barrier details, callouts, or lines indicating the installation of root barriers shown on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1473,"outputTokens":906,"totalTokens":4722,"reasoningTokens":2343},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements b