{"level":30,"time":1776445700308,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus specifically on the trees shown on the landscape plan near the overhead electric (OHE) line that runs along the southern boundary. 1) Identify all tree symbols along or near the OHE line. 2) For each tree, note whether it appears to be marked with a symbol like \"SY\" (street yard), \"PL\" (parking lot), \"P\" (parking buffer point), or \"M\" (mitigation tree). 3) Estimate the distance/clearance between the tree canopy circles and the OHE line - are the trees very close, touching, or with clear space? 4) Are there any trees planted on the southern property boundary itself near the OHE line? Be very specific about tree locations relative to buildings (Building 1-8) and the OHE line path.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the detailed information regarding the trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line:\n\n**1. Identification of the OHE Line and Tree Symbols**\nAn overhead electric line is clearly marked along the southern edge of the site, labeled with a dashed line text reading **\"- - OHE - -\"**. This line runs roughly parallel to the southern property boundary and the \"LOC\" (Limit of Construction) line. There are two distinct groupings of newly planted tree symbols situated directly along this path.\n\n**2. Tree Designations (SY, PL, P, M)**\nEvery clearly identifiable newly planted tree symbol located along this southern OHE line path is labeled with an \"**M**\". According to the KEY NOTES legend on the right side of the page, **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n\n**3. Distance/Clearance to the OHE Line**\nBased on the drawn symbols, there is **no clear space** between the planned tree canopies and the overhead electric line. In both the western and eastern clusters along the southern boundary, the circular symbols representing the tree canopies **directly intersect and overlap** the dashed \"- - OHE - -\" line.\n\n**4. Location on Boundary Relative to Buildings**\nWhile explicit labels for \"Building 1-8\" are not visible on this specific sheet, there is a large, continuous building structure running horizontally across the lower-middle portion of the site. The trees in question are planted in the narrow strip of land directly between the southern face of this main building structure and the southern property line/OHE path.\n\n*   **Southwest Cluster:** There is a group of three mitigation trees (\"M\") planted south of the western half of the southern building structure. All three canopies overlap the OHE line.\n*   **Southeast Cluster:** There is another group of three mitigation trees (\"M\") planted south of the eastern end of the southern building structure, near the southeast corner of the site plan. All three of these canopies also overlap the OHE line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1477,"outputTokens":427,"totalTokens":4717,"reasoningTokens":2813},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that p