th 'M') planted directly under and within 10 lateral feet of the overhead electric distribution line (---OHE---) running along the southern property boundary. Tree species are not identified on the landscape plan and cannot be verified against the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list in ECM Appendix F. According to UCM § 1.10.10.4, trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission lines or within 10 lateral feet of distribution lines must be utility-compatible species with mature height ≤20 feet, or have documented alternative mitigation. No such documentation is provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site Plan Release Notes do not include the required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Plans show overhead electric distribution lines adjacent to the property, and construction will occur nearby, triggering this notification requirement per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1649,"cache_read_input_tokens":64404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1649},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f309802-c1eb-4364-b84a-07fe4c2517f2","uuid":"152ad922-61b5-4c2d-914e-d4bdd37266eb"}
