{"level":30,"time":1776445825194,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZeL2YjeTVL8k7sbpDonqz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — Elevation view drawings of a typical step in a footing, showing dimensions and requirements for the bottom of strip footing to be level, stepping bottom of footing as required.\n     4→\n     5→2'-0\"\n     6→AS REQUIRED\n     7→#4 @ 12\" O.C.E.W.\n     8→BOTTOM OF STRIP FOOTING TO BE LEVEL, STEP BOTTOM OF FOOTING AS REQ'D.\n     9→2'-0\"\n    10→12\"\n    11→SEE \"RETAINING WALL\" DETAILS FOR FOOTING REINFORCING\n    12→ELEVATION VIEW\n    13→TYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\n    14→\n    15→## Block 2: diagram — A cross-section detail showing how to install a new slab adjacent to an existing slab using a #6 rebar dowel. It includes instructions for cleaning the surface, drilling holes, and inserting the rebar with epoxy.\n    16→\n    17→EXISTING SLAB\n    18→CLEAN EXISTING SURFACE PRIOR TO SETTING \"NEW\" CONCRETE\n    19→NEW SLAB\n    20→#6 REBAR (NOT SMOOTH DOWEL)\n    21→DRILL HOLE WITH 7/8\" BIT WHEN USING #4 REBAR\n    22→CLEAR HOLE WITH COMPRESSED AIR PRIOR TO INSERTING EPOXY.\n    23→6\" EMBED\n    24→DRILLED HOLE IN EXISTING CONCRETE SHOULD BE SIZED TO ALLOW REBAR INSTALLATION BY HAND. ONLY LIGHT \"TAPPING\" WITH HAMMER SHOULD BE REQUIRED.\n    25→DOWEL DETAIL\n    26→\n    27→## Block 3: diagram — A cross-section detail of a retaining wall with a maximum height of 14'-0\". It includes specifications for rebar placement, gravel backfill, geotextile fabric, weep pipes, and dimensions for the wall and footing.\n    28→\n    29→CHAMFER EXPOSED EDGES (TYPICAL)\n    30→EXISTING WALL\n    31→GRAVEL BACK FILL\n    32→#7 @ 10\" O.C. VERT.\n    33→14'-0\" MAX.\n    34→MIRAFI 140N GEOTEXTILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\n    35→#4 @ 12\" O.C. VERT.\n    36→#3 @ 12\" O.C. HORIZ. EACH FACE\n    37→ADD 2\" DIA. PVC WEEP PIPE @ 5' O.C. 8\" ABOVE WALL FOOTING \"TOE\"\n    38→TOP OF GRADE\n    39→#7 @ 10\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM\n    40→ADD (2)#6 DOWELS @ 18\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM SEE DETAIL THIS PAGE.\n    41→#4 @ 12\" O.C. CONT. AS SHOWN\n    42→14'-0\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\n    43→\n    44→## Block 4: drawing — A plan view drawing of retaining walls, pond walls, and existing walls. It includes callouts for a new retaining wall to be in place prior to demo for pond walls, an existing buttress with instructions to drill and epoxy #6 x 12\" dowels 6\" into the buttress 12\" O.C. tie to wall steel, and a callout to start on the south side of existing wall.\n    45→\n    46→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    47→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    48→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    49→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    50→NEW WALL TO BE IN PLACE PRIOR TO DEMO FOR POND WALLS.\n    51→NEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\n    52→EXISTING WALL\n    53→EXISTING BUTTRESS DRILL AND EPOXY #6 X 12\" DOWELS 6\" INTO BUTTRESS 12\" O.C. TIE TO WALL STEEL\n    54→NEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\n    55→PLAN VIEW\n    56→ONE 20' SECTION OF NEW FOOTING TO BE INSTALLED AT A TIME. START AT THE SOUTH SIDE OF EXISTING WALL.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 5: notes — A general note regarding the purpose of the schematic plan, confirming it is for locating and identifying foundation reinforcing elements only, and emphasizing the architect's responsibility for dimensional control.\n    59→\n    60→NOTE:\n    61→THIS IS A SCHEMATIC PLAN FOR THE PURPOSE OF LOCATING AND IDENTIFYING FOUNDATION REINFORCING ELEMENTS ONLY. VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS, DROPS, OFFSETS AND FEATURES WITH THE ARCHITECTURAL PLANS BEFORE FORMING THE FOUNDATION. MLAW CANNOT BE HELD LIABLE FOR ANY CONTRACTOR OVERSIGHT IN THIS REGARD. DO NOT FORM FOUNDATION USING THESE PLANS. DIMENSIONAL CONTROL IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE ARCHITECT. USE THESE PLANS FOR THE PLACEMENT OF THE GRADE BEAMS AND REINFORCEMENT.\n    62→\n    63→## Block 6: notes — A list of notes covering general contractor responsibilities, concrete specifications, and reinforcement requirements.\n    64→\n    65→NOTES:\n    66→1. THE CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR OBTAINING ALL PERMITS NECESSARY TO LEGALLY COMMENCE WITH THIS WORK.\n    67→2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\n    68→3. CONTRACTOR SHALL DISPOSE OF ALL SPOILS LEGALLY AT AN OFFSITE LOCATION OR AS DIRECTED BY OWNER.\n    69→4. SHOULD CONDITIONS ARISE THAT ARE NOT COVERED BY DETAILS ON THIS PLAN, CONTACT ENGINEER AT ONCE FOR ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS.\n    70→CONCRETE:\n    71→1. CONCRETE TO HAVE A MINIMUM 28 DAY COMPRESSIVE STRENGTH OF 3000 PSI.\n    72→2. CONCRETE SHALL BE WELL CONSOLIDATED USING PROPER MECHANICAL VIBRATION.\n    73→3. MINIMUM CONCRETE CLEAR COVER SHALL BE\n    74→IN SLABS:\n    75→3/4\" ADJACENT TO INTERIOR SLAB SURFACES\n    76→1 1/2\" ABOVE SUB-GRADE\n    77→IN STIFFENING BEAMS, WALLS AND FOOTINGS:\n    78→1 1/2\" ADJACENT TO EXTERIOR OR INTERIOR SURFACES\n    79→3\" FROM SURFACES IN CONTACT WITH EARTH\n    80→AT PIPE PENETRATION IN BEAM OR SLAB:\n    81→2\" FOR REBAR\n    82→REINFORCEMENT:\n    83→1. REINFORCING STEEL TO BE GRADE 60 FOR #4 AND LARGER AND GRADE 40 FOR #3.\n    84→2. ADD 24\"x24\" CORNER BARS EQUAL TO SIZE AND SPACING OF DISCONTINUOUS HORIZ. STEEL.\n    85→\n    86→## Block 9: table — A list of required inspections prior to specific construction phases.\n    87→\n    88→REQUIRED INSPECTIONS:\n    89→1. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF FOOTINGS.\n    90→2. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF WALLS.\n    91→3. PRIOR TO BACKFILL PLACEMENT TO VERIFY FILTER FABRIC AND DRAINAGE GRAVEL.\n    92→\n    93→## Block 10: table — A table outlining the design criteria for the project, including allowable soil bearing, lateral pressure method, active soil pressure for the heel, passive pressure, and soil weight.\n    94→\n    95→DESIGN CRITERIA:\n    96→REQUIREMENTS OF IBC 2015\n    97→| *ALLOWABLE SOIL BEARING | : 4,000 PSF |\n    98→|---|---|\n    99→| *LATERAL PRESSURE METHOD | : E.F.P. |\n   100→| *ACTIVE SOIL PRESSURE - HEEL | : 45.5 PSF |\n   101→| *PASSIVE PRESSURE | : 290 PSF |\n   102→| *SOIL WEIGHT | : 130 PSF |\n   103→\n   104→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f309802-c1eb-4364-b84a-07fe4c2517f2","uuid":"01714293-d7b3-42d6-9153-280b3ff638f2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — Elevation view drawings of a typical step in a footing, showing dimensions and requirements for the bottom of strip footing to be level, stepping bottom of footing as required.\n\n2'-0\"\nAS REQUIRED\n#4 @ 12\" O.C.E.W.\nBOTTOM OF STRIP FOOTING TO BE LEVEL, STEP BOTTOM OF FOOTING AS REQ'D.\n2'-0\"\n12\"\nSEE \"RETAINING WALL\" DETAILS FOR FOOTING REINFORCING\nELEVATION VIEW\nTYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A cross-section detail showing how to install a new slab adjacent to an existing slab using a #6 rebar dowel. It includes instructions for cleaning the surface, drilling holes, and inserting the rebar with epoxy.\n\nEXISTING SLAB\nCLEAN EXISTING SURFACE PRIOR TO SETTING \"NEW\" CONCRETE\nNEW SLAB\n#6 REBAR (NOT SMOOTH DOWEL)\nDRILL HOLE WITH 7/8\" BIT WHEN USING #4 REBAR\nCLEAR HOLE WITH COMPRESSED AIR PRIOR TO INSERTING EPOXY.\n6\" EMBED\nDRILLED HOLE IN EXISTING CONCRETE SHOULD BE SIZED TO ALLOW REBAR INSTALLATION BY HAND. ONLY LIGHT \"TAPPING\" WITH HAMMER SHOULD BE REQUIRED.\nDOWEL DETAIL\n\n## Block 3: diagram — A cross-section detail of a retaining wall with a maximum height of 14'-0\". It includes specifications for rebar placement, gravel backfill, geotextile fabric, weep pipes, and dimensions for the wall and footing.\n\nCHAMFER EXPOSED EDGES (TYPICAL)\nEXISTING WALL\nGRAVEL BACK FILL\n#7 @ 10\" O.C. VERT.\n14'-0\" MAX.\nMIRAFI 140N GEOTEXTILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\n#4 @ 12\" O.C. VERT.\n#3 @ 12\" O.C. HORIZ. EACH FACE\nADD 2\" DIA. PVC WEEP PIPE @ 5' O.C. 8\" ABOVE WALL FOOTING \"TOE\"\nTOP OF GRADE\n#7 @ 10\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM\nADD (2)#6 DOWELS @ 18\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM SEE DETAIL THIS PAGE.\n#4 @ 12\" O.C. CONT. AS SHOWN\n14'-0\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\n\n## Block 4: drawing — A plan view drawing of retaining walls, pond walls, and existing walls. It includes callouts for a new retaining wall to be in place prior to demo for pond walls, an existing buttress with instructions to drill and epoxy #6 x 12\" dowels 6\" into the buttress 12\" O.C. tie to wall steel, and a callout to start on the south side of existing wall.\n\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nNEW WALL TO BE IN PLACE PRIOR TO DEMO FOR POND WALLS.\nNEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\nEXISTING WALL\nEXISTING BUTTRESS DRILL AND EPOXY #6 X 12\" DOWELS 6\" INTO BUTTRESS 12\" O.C. TIE TO WALL STEEL\nNEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\nPLAN VIEW\nONE 20' SECTION OF NEW FOOTING TO BE INSTALLED AT A TIME. START AT THE SOUTH SIDE OF EXISTING WALL.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A general note regarding the purpose of the schematic plan, confirming it is for locating and identifying foundation reinforcing elements only, and emphasizing the architect's responsibility for dimensional control.\n\nNOTE:\nTHIS IS A SCHEMATIC PLAN FOR THE PURPOSE OF LOCATING AND IDENTIFYING FOUNDATION REINFORCING ELEMENTS ONLY. VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS, DROPS, OFFSETS AND FEATURES WITH THE ARCHITECTURAL PLANS BEFORE FORMING THE FOUNDATION. MLAW CANNOT BE HELD LIABLE FOR ANY CONTRACTOR OVERSIGHT IN THIS REGARD. DO NOT FORM FOUNDATION USING THESE PLANS. DIMENSIONAL CONTROL IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE ARCHITECT. USE THESE PLANS FOR THE PLACEMENT OF THE GRADE BEAMS AND REINFORCEMENT.\n\n## Block 6: notes — A list of notes covering general contractor responsibilities, concrete specifications, and reinforcement requirements.\n\nNOTES:\n1. THE CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR OBTAINING ALL PERMITS NECESSARY TO LEGALLY COMMENCE WITH THIS WORK.\n2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\n3. CONTRACTOR SHALL DISPOSE OF ALL SPOILS LEGALLY AT AN OFFSITE LOCATION OR AS DIRECTED BY OWNER.\n4. SHOULD CONDITIONS ARISE THAT ARE NOT COVERED BY DETAILS ON THIS PLAN, CONTACT ENGINEER AT ONCE FOR ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS.\nCONCRETE:\n1. CONCRETE TO HAVE A MINIMUM 28 DAY COMPRESSIVE STRENGTH OF 3000 PSI.\n2. CONCRETE SHALL BE WELL CONSOLIDATED USING PROPER MECHANICAL VIBRATION.\n3. MINIMUM CONCRETE CLEAR COVER SHALL BE\nIN SLABS:\n3/4\" ADJACENT TO INTERIOR SLAB SURFACES\n1 1/2\" ABOVE SUB-GRADE\nIN STIFFENING BEAMS, WALLS AND FOOTINGS:\n1 1/2\" ADJACENT TO EXTERIOR OR INTERIOR SURFACES\n3\" FROM SURFACES IN CONTACT WITH EARTH\nAT PIPE PENETRATION IN BEAM OR SLAB:\n2\" FOR REBAR\nREINFORCEMENT:\n1. REINFORCING STEEL TO BE GRADE 60 FOR #4 AND LARGER AND GRADE 40 FOR #3.\n2. ADD 24\"x24\" CORNER BARS EQUAL TO SIZE AND SPACING OF DISCONTINUOUS HORIZ. STEEL.\n\n## Block 9: table — A list of required inspections prior to specific construction phases.\n\nREQUIRED INSPECTIONS:\n1. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF FOOTINGS.\n2. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF WALLS.\n3. PRIOR TO BACKFILL PLACEMENT TO VERIFY FILTER FABRIC AND DRAINAGE GRAVEL.\n\n## Block 10: table — A table outlining the design criteria for the project, including allowable soil bearing, lateral pressure method, active soil pressure for the heel, passive pressure, and soil weight.\n\nDESIGN CRITERIA:\nREQUIREMENTS OF IBC 2015\n| *ALLOWABLE SOIL BEARING | : 4,000 PSF |\n|---|---|\n| *LATERAL PRESSURE METHOD | : E.F.P. |\n| *ACTIVE SOIL PRESSURE - HEEL | : 45.5 PSF |\n| *PASSIVE PRESSURE | : 290 PSF |\n| *SOIL WEIGHT | : 130 PSF |\n\n","numLines":104,"startLine":1,"totalLines":104}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776445825194,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013QeQpNgjYVXW9dGwAdytFp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The wall plan sheets show structural details for the retaining walls but do NOT show any clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines. The sections show the wall cross-section (up to 14 feet high) and reinforcement details, but there's no mention of overhead line clearances.\n\nSo I should add items EL-1.14 and EL-1.17 to the findings as \"not-verifiable\" since:\n- EL-1.14: Retaining walls do not maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line - NOT VERIFIABLE (no clearance dimensions shown)\n- EL-1.17: Retaining walls lack section exhibits showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall - NOT VERIFIABLE (sections don't show overhead lines or clearances)\n\nNow let me also check if I need to add any other items. Let me think about the other key elements:\n\n1. **Fences** (EL-1.9, EL-1.10) - Fences appear to be shown on the site plan and existing conditions survey, but no clearance dimensions are provided for either the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance or the 10-foot post-to-pole distance. These would be \"not-verifiable.\"\n\n2. **Sidewalks** (EL-1.25) - The vision analysis mentioned sidewalks and pathways are shown on the site plan. There are sidewalks adjacent to the perimeter. However, the specific instruction is \"Sidewalks not cleared from existing power poles at each end of property along right-of-way.\" The poles are shown outside the property line (on ROW). Without specific dimensions showing the sidewalk is clear of the poles, this is not-verifiable.\n\n3. **Water meters and water lines** (EL-1.28, EL-1.29) - The utility plan shows water lines and meters, but no clearance dimensions from overhead service drops or distribution lines. Not-verifiable.\n\n\n4. **Meter obstruction** (EL-1.38) - Meters are shown on plans, but without an enlarged detail showing the meter area and surrounding features, cannot verify whether obstructions exist. Not-verifiable.\n\n5. **Service mast through roof** (EL-1.47) - Need to check if service mastsare shown on the utility plan. Without detailed dimensions, would be not-verifiable.\n\n6. **Down guys** (EL-1.40, EL-1.42) - The existing survey mentions \"guy wires\" and the legend includes symbols for guy anchors. But these haven't been explicitly confirmed in conflict with proposed features. From the vision analysis, there was mention of a pole with guy wires, but I need to verify if the proposed work creates any conflicts with these existing guy anchors or if they're positioned safely away from construction areas.\n\nLooking at what I can definitively mark as not-verifiable based on missing documentation: building elevations with surveyed conductor elevations, section/plan exhibits with clearance dimensions, retaining wall clearances and sections, driveway vertical clearance, and clearance dimensions from conductors all lack the necessary detail or exhibits to confirm compliance.\n\nSeveral items clearly fail outright—trees that aren't utility-compatible, the missing 48-hour notification requirement, and clearance from the pole itself. Beyond these core deficiencies, there are additional gaps I should flag: fence clearance dimensions aren't shown, fence post distances from poles lack verification, sidewalk clearances from poles aren't documented, water meter and water line clearances from service infrastructure aren't addressed, and survey documentation showing pole locations appears incomplete.\n\nHowever, I need to be selective about what constitutes a genuine conflict versus items that may not actually be in the overhead lines' path. The overhead lines run along the site's west and east boundaries, so interior features like sidewalks might not create actual conflicts. I should prioritize the most defensible violations—those with clear documentation gaps or direct conflicts with the overhead infrastructure shown on the plans.\n\nThe retaining walls adjacent to the southern overhead lines and the missing survey data are worth flagging. My core six findings capture the essential deficiencies: building elevations lacking surveyed conductor data, section/plan exhibits without clearance dimensions, the driveway crossing issue, and several other critical verification gaps that directly impact safety compliance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":72423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2434},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f309802-c1eb-4364-b84a-07fe4c2517f2","uuid":"4d214bf6-6740-403d-8330-022347c3ee1f"}
