{"level":30,"time":1776445825195,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019zs4EcEiz2XT8RPbttT2rJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Engineer's Summary Letter\n     2→\n     3→An engineer's summary letter detailing existing conditions, proposed improvements, and utilities for the project site plan.\n     4→\n     5→## Sections\n     6→\n     7→1. **Header and Introduction** (p. 1)\n     8→   Document header, addressee, and introductory statement identifying the summary letter for the proposed townhome development.\n     9→   File: `01-header-and-introduction.md`\n    10→2. **General Information** (p. 1)\n    11→   Provides the site location details, including watershed, floodplain status, aquifer zone, and zoning information for the project.\n    12→   File: `02-general-information.md`\n    13→3. **Existing Conditions** (p. 1)\n    14→   Describes the current state of the site, noting existing impervious cover, drainage patterns, and easements.\n    15→   File: `03-existing-conditions.md`\n    16→4. **Proposed Project** (p. 1)\n    17→   Outlines the proposed construction of 39 townhomes, water quality controls, and a reduction in impervious cover.\n    18→   File: `04-proposed-project.md`\n    19→5. **Utilities** (p. 2)\n    20→   Details the planned water and wastewater connections for the project's eight buildings and includes the engineer's sign-off.\n    21→   File: `05-utilities.md`\n    22→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baebfa71-225a-4ef1-87a6-157059cbeeb0","uuid":"7b78dc01-d2d8-4d63-812e-246eaf8acd0f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/engineer-s-summary-letter/overview.md","content":"# Engineer's Summary Letter\n\nAn engineer's summary letter detailing existing conditions, proposed improvements, and utilities for the project site plan.\n\n## Sections\n\n1. **Header and Introduction** (p. 1)\n   Document header, addressee, and introductory statement identifying the summary letter for the proposed townhome development.\n   File: `01-header-and-introduction.md`\n2. **General Information** (p. 1)\n   Provides the site location details, including watershed, floodplain status, aquifer zone, and zoning information for the project.\n   File: `02-general-information.md`\n3. **Existing Conditions** (p. 1)\n   Describes the current state of the site, noting existing impervious cover, drainage patterns, and easements.\n   File: `03-existing-conditions.md`\n4. **Proposed Project** (p. 1)\n   Outlines the proposed construction of 39 townhomes, water quality controls, and a reduction in impervious cover.\n   File: `04-proposed-project.md`\n5. **Utilities** (p. 2)\n   Details the planned water and wastewater connections for the project's eight buildings and includes the engineer's sign-off.\n   File: `05-utilities.md`\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
