{"level":30,"time":1776445825196,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01H4bqbmcQoEFuYzA1o9MKXH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have very concrete information:\n\n**Trees near the OHE line on the southern boundary:**\n1. One \"M\" (Mitigation) tree - approximately 5 feet from the OHE line, species NOT labeled\n2. One \"SY\" (Street Yard) tree - west of the M tree\n3. One \"P\" (Parking Buffer Point) tree - east of the M tree\n4. ALL THREE have canopy circles that cross/overlap the OHE line\n\nThis is a CRITICAL finding because:\n- These are NEW proposed trees\n- At least one (\"M\") is within 10 feet of the OHE line (at ~5 feet)\n- Their canopies cross the line\n- The species are NOT identified on the landscape plan\n- Without knowing the species, I cannot verify if they are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n\nLet me now think about what checklist items apply:\n\n**EL-1.37** - Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are not from Utility Compatible Shade Trees list\n- The M tree at ~5 feet is DEFINITELY within 10 feet\n- The species is not identified\n- The canopy crosses the line\n- This is a FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\nI also need to check:\n1. Whether there are clearance dimensions for the overhead lines (EL-1.23 - clearances measured from conductor vs pole) - I found NO clearance dimensions labeled\n2. Whether there are surveyed elevations showing overhead conductor locations (EL-1.7) - need to check if any building elevation sheets exist\n3. Whether there's a 48-hour notification note (EL-1.46)\n4. Whether overhead lines appear to be under buildings/structures (EL-1.27 - prohibition against structures under/over distribution lines)\n\nLet me check the cover sheet and see if there's a 48-hour notification note, and also look