{"level":30,"time":1776445825197,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017CHadHrox6Ujd65CD3sqjA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, there are 39 sheets total as listed in the README. Now let me check the readme to see what sheets 22-39 are about. Looking back at my earlier read of the README, I see:\n- Sheet 22: Construction Details 1 (curbs, sidewalks, driveways)\n- Sheet 23-28: Construction Details (water, fire, wastewater, storm drain)\n- Sheet 29: Addressing Plan\n- Sheet 30-37: Landscape/Tree-related\n- Sheet 38-39: Wall Plans\n\nI don't see any \"Building Elevation\" sheets listed. So there are NO surveyed building elevation sheets showing overhead conductors and clearances.\n\nLet me now compile my findings and determine which checklist items to flag as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\nBased on my research:\n\n**RESEARCH PHASE FINDINGS:**\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Infrastructure**:\n   - Sheet 4 shows O.H.U.L. (overhead utility lines) on three sides of property\n   - Sheet 31 shows overhead electric (OHE) line on southern boundary\n   - No specific voltage designation visible (but facts mention electric easements)\n   - Multiple utility poles documented\n\n2. **New Tree Plantings Near Overhead Lines**:\n   - Sheet 31 shows three new trees very close to southern OHE line:\n     - One \"M\" (Mitigation) tree ~5 feet from line\n     - One \"SY\" (Street Yard) tree west of M tree\n     - One \"P\" (Parking Buffer Point) tree east of M tree\n   - Tree canopies cross the OHE line\n   - Tree SPECIES ARE NOT IDENTIFIED on landscape plan\n   - Cannot verify utility compatibility without species identification\n\n3. **Clearance Documentation**:\n   - NO clearance dimensions shown from OHE line to any site features\n   - No surveyed conductor elevations or building elevation sheets with overhead lines visible\n   - No section/profile views showing vertical clearances to structures\n   - No notes documenting measurements taken from the actual conductor rather than the pole\n\n4. **Electrical Design**:\n   - Sheet 21 shows NEW underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, meters, pull boxes)\n   - No overhead distribution mentioned for NEW work\n   - But existing overhead lines remain on property and adjacent\n\n5. **General Notes**:\n   - No 48-hour notification note found on cover sheet\n   - General utility disclaimer on multiple sheets about field verification\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:\n\n**EL-1.1** - Buildings\n\nBuildings and permanent structures appear to maintain adequate clearance from overhead conductors. The structures are positioned well away from the OHE line, with the nearest building located over 100 feet to the north. No structures sit directly beneath or immediately adjacent to the overhead line. This item passes.\n\n**EL-1.2** - Customer facilities do not maintain 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral conductors\n\nNew electrical infrastructure shown on Sheet 21 lacks documented clearance dimensions from the OHE line. However, the new transformers, meters, and other equipment appear to be part of underground or interior electrical systems rather than positioned near the overhead line. Full verification isn't possible without more detailed utility coordination drawings.\n\n**EL-1.3** - Building projections do not maintain clearances\n\nNo building projections like overhangs, awnings, or balconies are visible near the OHE line. This item passes based on the current site layout.\n\n**EL-1.4** - Gas pump canopies do not maintain clearances\n\nNo gas pump facilities exist on the site. Not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.5** - Stairs, elevated walkways, elevated platforms do not maintain clearances\n\nNo elevated structures of this type are positioned near the OHE line. This item passes.\n\n**EL-1.6** - Buildings do not maintain clearances from OH facilities in ROW\n\nThe buildings sit north of the property, well removed from the OHE line located on the southern boundary within what appears to be a ROW or easement. This item passes.\n\n**EL-1.7** - Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors not included on building elevation sheets\n\nNo building elevation sheets are provided in this plan set, and no surveyed conductor elevations are documented. Cannot verify.\n\n**EL-1.8** - Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer conductor to building edges\n\nNo section views are provided that would show clearance dimensions between the overhead line and building edges.\n\nBuildings appear sufficiently distant that this requirement may not apply, though the item would pass if structures maintain greater than 15 feet separation.\n\n**EL-1.9** - Fences do not maintain 7.5-foot clearance from OH conductors\n\nSheet 31 shows fences near property boundaries where the OHE line is located on the southern boundary. No clearance dimensions are provided to verify the required separation. Cannot verify.\n\n**EL-1.10** - Fence posts do not maintain 10-foot clearance from overhead poles\n\nBoth fence posts and utility poles appear on the property boundaries without documented clearance dimensions. Cannot verify.\n\n**EL-1.11** - Fences connecting to substation fences not electrically isolated\n\nNo substation is shown on the plans. Not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.12** - Fencing near transmission lines not constructed of non-conductive material\n\nThe plans indicate distribution lines only, not transmission lines at 60kV or higher. Not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.13** - Vehicle barrier fencing beneath OH lines lacks clearance verification\n\nNo vehicle barrier fencing appears beneath the OHE line. Not applicable or passes.\n\n**EL-1.14** - Retaining walls do not maintain 7.5-foot clearance\n\nRetaining wall details are shown on Sheets 38-39. Need to cross-reference the grading plan to determine if any walls are positioned near the OHE line.\n\n**EL-1.15** - Retaining walls adjacent to substation walls lack 5-foot separation\n\nNo substation is shown. Not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.16** - Emergency access structures lack clearances\n\nNo such structures are shown. Not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.17** - Retaining walls lack section exhibits showing clearance dimensions\n\nWall details appear on Sheets 38-39, but I need to verify whether they include clearance dimensions relative to the OHE line. Status depends on wall positioning relative to the overhead line.\n\n**EL-1.18** - Driveways do not maintain 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance\n\nDriveways are located on Sheet 31. The OHE line runs south of the driveway area, but no vertical clearance measurements are provided. Cannot verify without height data.\n\n**EL-1.19** - Vehicles parked on concrete pads don't maintain clearance\n\nParking pads are shown on Sheet 31 with the OHE line positioned to the south. Vertical clearance dimensions are not provided, so this cannot be verified.\n\n**EL-1.20** - Roads/driveways don't maintain 30-foot clearance from transmission lines\n\nThis would only be relevant if transmission lines exist on the site. Likely not applicable.\n\n**EL-1.21** - Highway/freeway grades don't maintain 40-foot clearance\n\nNot applicable—this is an urban townhome project, not a highway or freeway.\n\n**EL-1.22** - Existing poles in conflict with driveways not relocated 30 feet\n\nPoles are shown on Sheet 4. The main building and driveway are interior to the site with no visible pole conflicts. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions measured from pole instead of conductor\n\nNo clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the plans, so proper dimension annotations are missing. This is a deficiency.\n\n**EL-1.24** - Streetlight poles located under OH lines\n\nNo streetlights are positioned beneath the overhead line. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.25** - Sidewalks not cleared from power poles at property ends\n\nSidewalks are shown on Sheet 31 and poles are at property boundaries, but there are no clearance conflicts. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.26** - Trash areas placed under OH facilities\n\nTrash enclosures are not positioned near the overhead line. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.27** - Customer facilities installed under/over distribution lines\n\nNo buildings or structures are located under or over the overhead line, which runs along the southern boundary while buildings are positioned to the north. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.28** - Water meters do not maintain clearance from OH service drops\n\nWater infrastructure needs to be evaluated for clearance from service drops.\n\n**EL-1.29** - Water lines don't maintain clearance from OH distribution\n\nWater lines are shown on the plans, but the relationship between them and the overhead line lacks dimensional verification. Cannot confirm without measurements.\n\n**EL-1.30** - Permanent foundations within 5 feet of property line\n\nBuildings are positioned well away from property lines with no foundations within the 5-foot setback. This passes.\n\n**EL-1.31** - Survey by registered surveyor for mid-span clearances not provided\n\nNo surveyor clearance documentation exists and overhead line heights are not dimensioned. Cannot verify without this data.\n\n**EL-1.32** - Overhead line crossings not at 90-degree angles\n\nThe single overhead line visible runs along the southern boundary in an east-west direction. Trees M, SY, and P are positioned within 5-10 feet of overhead electrical lines, but their species aren't identified on the plans, making it impossible to confirm they're from the Utility Compatible list—this is a critical gap. STATUS: FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\nMeter locations appear unobstructed on Sheet 21. No conflicts with existing streetlights are evident. Guy wire documentation is unclear, though driveway placement doesn't seem to create conflicts with pole locations.\n\nThe new transformers shown are underground or pad-mounted, so they meet the 7.5-foot and 35-foot vertical clearance requirements. Guy anchor easements aren't documented on the plans, so verification isn't possible if such anchors are required.\n\nNo construction staging plan was provided, making it impossible to verify the 10-foot radial clearance requirement. The cover sheet is missing the required 48-hour notification note. Building elevation sheets aren't included in the set, so I can't verify service-mast clearances through roof penetrations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":177,"cache_read_input_tokens":80663,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":177},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"0420a1bf-a1bb-49ab-a83f-95ee489e60f0"}
