{"level":30,"time":1776445945275,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJa5cCxKt9hBxW49p4oFBr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 20\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Transmission Notes\n     6→1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n     7→2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n     8→3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n     9→4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    11→6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n    12→7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n    13→8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n    14→9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n    15→10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    16→11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n    17→12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n    18→13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n    19→14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n    20→15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n    21→16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    22→  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    23→  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    24→  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"eea1eb5c-a827-40f1-b054-9216fa133986","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-20.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 20\n\n## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n\nElectric Transmission Notes\n1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776445945275,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GWkTpW4gDDnmK5RZpLy6Xy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I found the 48-hour notification note on Sheet 3 (General Notes), Block 20, Item 3: \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.\"\n\nHowever, I need to check if this note distinguishes between transmission and distribution lines. The grouping EL-1.46 requires the note to reference \"48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines\" per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.\n\nLooking at the notes, they are labeled \"Electric Transmission Notes\" and specifically reference transmission facilities and structures. The note mentions \"transmission wire\" and \"transmission structures\" throughout.\n\nThe issue is that the note appears to apply ONLY to transmission facilities (≥60kV), not distribution facilities (<60kV). For distribution lines, the requirement would also apply per the grouping description.\n\nBut I need to check - does the property have transmission lines or just distribution lines?\n\nLooking back at my findings:\n- Sheet 4 shows \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" but doesn't specify voltage\n- Sheet 31 shows \"-OHE-\" (Overhead Electric) but doesn't specify voltage\n- The facts.md mentioned \"5' ELECTRIC EASEMENTS\" which are typically for distribution, not transmission\n- Sheet 3 transmission notes mention 25' grading restriction and transmission structures - these are much larger than distribution\n\nIt's unclear whether TRANSMISSION lines or just DISTRIBUTION lines are present. The electrical design (Sheet 21) shows underground service, so maybe the main voltage supply is underground.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the transmission notes on Sheet 3, they seem very specific to transmission structures and require 25-foot clearances and transmission easements. These notes may be standard boilerplate for any project that touches transmission infrastructure, even if transmission doesn't directly affect this site.\n\nLet me reconsider: The grouping EL-1.46 states the requirement applies \"Only when overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to site and construction activities are proposed.\"\n\n\nSince overhead lines do exist on the plans and construction is proposed, the 48-hour notification requirement applies. The note is present on Sheet 3, though it's framed within the transmission section. The substance addresses the Austin Energy notification requirement 48 hours before construction begins. I should verify whether this transmission-specific language satisfies EL-1.46 or if the note needs to explicitly cover distribution lines as well, since the grouping instructions require the owner to be notified before work near overhead lines.\n\nThe note on Sheet 3 states a pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy is required 48 hours before construction commences, with Andrew Perez listed as the contact. This appears to meet the requirement despite its transmission focus, so EL-1.46 should be marked as passing.\n\nNow I can move through the remaining items. Several are clearly not applicable: no gas pumps present for EL-1.4, no substation for EL-1.11 and EL-1.15, no transmission fencing or non-conductive fencing for EL-1.12, and no emergency access structures for EL-1.16.\n\nAdditional items don't apply to this project—no transmission lines or highway grades for EL-1.20 and EL-1.21, no marquee signage for EL-1.34, underground electrical eliminating new power poles for EL-1.35, and no down guy anchors shown for EL-1.41 and EL-1.42.\n\nFor items that pass, the buildings and structures maintain adequate distance from overhead electrical lines per EL-1.1, EL-1.3, EL-1.5, and EL-1.6. Multiple other items show no conflicts—EL-1.22, EL-1.24 through EL-1.27, EL-1.30, EL-1.38, and EL-1.39 all check out. The new electrical transformers are underground per EL-1.43 and EL-1.44.\n\nThe Austin Energy 48-hour notification requirement on Sheet 3 is satisfied for EL-1.46. However, several items cannot be verified: EL-1.7 lacks building elevation sheets showing surveyed conductor elevations, EL-1.8 has no section views documenting clearances from outer conductors to buildings, and EL-1.9 cannot be confirmed since fences near the southern boundary lack clearance dimensions—this could potentially fail depending on actual distances.\n\nSimilarly, EL-1.10 shows fence posts positioned near poles on property boundaries without dimensional documentation. Retaining walls exist but lack section exhibits with clearance measurements relative to overhead equipment, making EL-1.17 unverifiable if walls are proximate to the line. The driveway on the southern portion near overhead facilities has no vertical clearance dimensions shown, so EL-1.18 cannot be assessed. For EL-1.23, since no clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the plans, I cannot determine whether measurements originate from poles or conductors—the fundamental problem is the complete absence of clearance documentation.\n\nWater lines shown on the plans lack any clearance dimensions relative to overhead distribution, leaving EL-1.29 unverifiable. EL-1.31 fails because no surveyed mid-span clearance data for overhead lines was provided. Three new trees planted within approximately 5 feet of the overhead line have canopies that cross into the line, but their species aren't identified on the landscape plan, so I cannot confirm they're from the Utility Compatible list—EL-1.37 fails on the missing survey requirement and cannot be verified regarding species compatibility.\n\nDown guy wires potentially exist on poles but aren't clearly shown or documented on the plans, making EL-1.40 unverifiable. Without a construction staging plan, I cannot assess whether staging areas maintain the required 10-foot clearance from overhead lines for EL-1.45. Building elevation sheets are absent, preventing verification of service-mast through-roof clearances for EL-1.47.\n\nFor the deficiency assessment, EL-1.31 represents an actual failure—surveyed mid-span clearance data wasn't provided. EL-1.37 also fails because trees within 10 feet of the overhead line have unidentified species. The remaining items—EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.9, EL-1.10, EL-1.17, EL-1.18, EL-1.23, EL-1.29, and EL-1.40—cannot be verified due to missing documentation: no building elevation sheets showing overhead conductors, no section views for clearances, no dimensional data for fences, fence posts, walls, driveways, water lines, or conductor clearances.\n\nEL-1.45 and EL-1.47 also fall into the not-verifiable category since construction staging plans and building elevation sheets weren't provided. Regarding EL-1.23 specifically, the requirement focuses on measurement methodology when dimensions exist—measured from pole versus conductor—so without any dimensions shown, verification becomes impossible rather than a direct violation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":86422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1267},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d610813-7074-4147-a1dd-09845ecb3b90","uuid":"caacf329-cdc0-49e9-91d1-551139183455"}
{"level":30,"time":1776445945275,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GWkTpW4gDDnmK5RZpLy6Xy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found the 48-hour notification note on Sheet 3 (General Notes). Now I have enough information to complete my evaluation. Let me compile my final findings.\n\nBased on my comprehensive research phase, I've identified the following key issues:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**FOUND / VERIFIED:**\n- Overhead utility lines on multiple sides of property (Sheet 4: north, west, south boundaries)\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) line on southern boundary with THREE new trees planted ~5 feet away (Sheet 31)\n- Tree canopies crossing the OHE line\n- **Tree species NOT identified** on landscape plan\n- Austin Energy 48-hour notification note present on Sheet 3\n- Electric easements documented on property\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to any site features (buildings, fences, driveways, walls)\n- Surveyed elevations/locations of overhead conductors\n- Building elevation sheets (none exist in this plan set)\n- Section/profile views showing vertical clearances from overhead lines\n- Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data\n- Down guy wire locations/documentation\n- Construction staging plan\n- Documentation of whether new trees meet utility-compatible requirements\n\nNow let me evaluate the checklist items and return findings for FAIL and NOT-VERIFIABLE items only:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":86422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1267},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use