ant, but no measurements shown\n\n6. **Tree and Vegetation Clearances (EL-13.13, EL-13.14, EL-13.15)**:\n   - The landscape plan fails to show transformer pad locations, making it impossible to verify tree and shrub clearances. No root barrier details are provided, and the tree list doesn't identify which species are positioned near the pads.\n\n7. **Utility Coordination**:\n   - The plans lack any documentation showing transformer pads maintain required 5-foot separations from water, wastewater, and storm drain lines. No utility separation measurements are provided.\n\n8. **Property Location and Easement Restrictions (EL-13.33, EL-13.34, EL-13.35, EL-13.36)**:\n   - NO clear indication that transformer pads are 100% on private property. TP-1 appears adjacent to or within a sidewalk easement, while TP-2 sits in a Vault Easement and TP-3 in a Drainage Easement—neither placement has documented AE approval. Transformer easements are absent from the plans, and no routing diagram shows electrical service from transformer to meters.\n\n9. **Grading and Drainage (EL-13.32)**:\n   - The Grading Plan omits transformer pad locations, preventing verification that drainage slopes away from the pads. The transformer type (oil-filled versus dry-type) remains unspecified.\n\n10. **Austin Energy Design Coordination**:\n    - Missing ESPA or Austin Energy Design approval documents. No evidence of coordination with Austin Energy Design or documented clearance reduction approvals for bollards, pads, and service type per EL-13.4 exceptions.\n\nNow evaluating each checklist item in detail.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":61848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3cb3ac19-