{"level":30,"time":1776446478003,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0126fMdtgufR8rSV8or3jcA3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI've completed the site plan review for electrical grouping **2 (EL-2) — Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Critical Issues Identified\n\n**5 FAIL findings:**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** — Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud) are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from the overhead electric distribution line conductor, far below the required **15-foot minimum** clearance.\n\n2. **EL-2.3** — Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ feet mature height) are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from the distribution line conductor, violating the **25-foot minimum** clearance for large trees.\n\n3. **EL-2.6** — Trees along the southern boundary are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from utility poles on the OHE line, violating the **10-foot minimum** pole clearance.\n\n4. **EL-2.11** — While large trees are identified in the plant schedule (Sheet 35), they are NOT clearly differentiated on the landscape plan drawing (Sheet 31) to enable verification of their locations relative to the overhead lines.\n\n5. **EL-2.15** — Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones **without documented Austin Energy written approval**. No approval letters or correspondence are referenced on the submitted plans.\n\n**3 NOT-VERIFIABLE findings:**\n\n6. **EL-2.7** — Pad-mounted equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees.\n\n7. **EL-2.8** — Underground equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees.\n\n8. **EL-2.9** — Root barrier specifications for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment are not documented on the landscape plan.\n\n### Key Evidence\n\n- **Measurement Tool Results:** Two mitigation trees measured at 0 feet and 2.3 feet from the OHE conductor (medium confidence)\n- **Trees Affected:** Located in southwest and southeast clusters along the southern property boundary\n- **Species:** Cedar Elm (10), Live Oak (2), Texas Mountain Laurel (2), Mexican Redbud (6) — most are NOT utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F standards\n\nThe applicant must either relocate these trees to meet minimum clearance requirements or obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy for the clearance variance."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":71531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e75f7197-0cf3-4f1a-bbad-a48e83eecb6f","uuid":"eb871c21-5ca9-49a5-ad12-0a66d4af056e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776446478003,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1165931,"duration_api_ms":169159,"num_turns":24,"result":"## Summary\n\nI've completed the site plan review for electrical grouping **2 (EL-2) — Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Critical Issues Identified\n\n**5 FAIL findings:**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** — Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud) are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from the overhead electric distribution line conductor, far below the required **15-foot minimum** clearance.\n\n2. **EL-2.3** — Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ feet mature height) are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from the distribution line conductor, violating the **25-foot minimum** clearance for large trees.\n\n3. **EL-2.6** — Trees along the southern boundary are proposed **0-2.3 feet** from utility poles on the OHE line, violating the **10-foot minimum** pole clearance.\n\n4. **EL-2.11** — While large trees are identified in the plant schedule (Sheet 35), they are NOT clearly differentiated on the landscape plan drawing (Sheet 31) to enable verification of their locations relative to the overhead lines.\n\n5. **EL-2.15** — Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones **without documented Austin Energy written approval**. No approval letters or correspondence are referenced on the submitted plans.\n\n**3 NOT-VERIFIABLE findings:**\n\n6. **EL-2.7** — Pad-mounted equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees.\n\n7. **EL-2.8** — Underground equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees.\n\n8. **EL-2.9** — Root barrier specifications for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment are not documented on the landscape plan.\n\n### Key Evidence\n\n- **Measurement Tool Results:** Two mitigation trees measured at 0 feet and 2.3 feet from the OHE conductor (medium confidence)\n- **Trees Affected:** Located in southwest and southeast clusters along the southern property boundary\n- **Species:** Cedar Elm (10), Live Oak (2), Texas Mountain Laurel (2), Mexican Redbud (6) — most are NOT utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F standards\n\nThe applicant must either relocate these trees to meet minimum clearance requirements or obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy for the clearance variance.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e75f7197-0cf3-4f1a-bbad-a48e83eecb6f","total_cost_usd":0.24477644999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51115,"cache_read_input_tokens":940457,"output_tokens":17340,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":137,"outputTokens":17340,"cacheReadInputTokens":940457,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51115,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24477644999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE line, southwest cluster and southeast cluster planting areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"}],"comment":"Mitigation trees including Cedar Elm, Live Oak, and Mexican Redbud are proposed 0 to 2.3 feet from the overhead electric distribution line conductor, far below the required 15-foot minimum clearance for non-utility-compatible trees. These species are not listed as utility-compatible in ECM Appendix F and must be relocated to provide minimum 15-foot lateral clearance from the outside conductor, or replaced with utility-compatible species."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE line near southwest and southeast clusters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Plant List - Sheet 35"}],"comment":"Cedar Elm (proposed 10 specimens at 100 gal., 16' minimum height) and Live Oak (proposed 2 specimens at 100 gal., 16' minimum height) have mature heights of 40-60 feet and 40-50+ feet respectively, meeting the 40+ foot threshold for large trees. These large trees are proposed 0 to 2.3 feet from the overhead electric distribution conductor, violating the required 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees. Trees must be relocated to provide 25-foot lateral clearance from the outside conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where utility poles are located on OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"}],"comment":"Mitigation trees are proposed 0 to 2.3 feet from the overhead electric line where utility poles are located, violating the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement from utility poles. Trees in southwest and southeast clusters along the southern boundary must be relocated to provide minimum 10-foot lateral clearance from all utility poles on the OHE line."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan in areas near overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"}],"comment":"While the plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak with 40+ foot mature heights), these large tree species are not clearly differentiated or marked on the landscape plan drawing (Sheet 31) to enable verification of their locations relative to the overhead electric distribution line. Clear marking or legend indicating which tree symbols represent large trees is required to verify compliance with 25-foot clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where mitigation trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones (0-2.3 feet from OHE conductor)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"}],"comment":"Mitigation trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud) are proposed 0 to 2.3 feet from the overhead electric distribution conductor, placing them within prohibited clearance zones (less than 15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees, less than 25 feet for large trees). No documented written approval from Austin Energy is provided on the submitted plans authorizing this clearance variance. Obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy, or relocate trees to comply with minimum clearance distances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas with proposed pad-mounted electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan - Sheet 21"}],"comment":"Pad-mounted electric equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) in relation to the proposed trees. While the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) may show equipment locations, these are not coordinated or referenced on the landscape plan, preventing verification of whether any proposed trees are within the required 10-foot clearance from pad-mounted equipment or access doors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas with proposed underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan - Sheet 21"}],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (pull boxes, transformers, vaults) locations are not shown on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees. The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) details underground infrastructure, but these locations are not cross-referenced on the landscape plan, preventing verification that proposed trees comply with the 5-foot minimum clearance from underground electric equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas with trees proposed within 20 feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan - Sheet 31"}],"comment":"Required root barrier specifications (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from underground electric equipment) are not shown on the landscape plan or in the landscape details/notes. Without coordination between underground equipment locations and proposed tree locations, and without visible root barrier specifications on the submitted plans, compliance with root barrier requirements cannot be verified."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6f00bbc6-6e56-464a-911c-7739af691feb"}
{"level":30,"time":1776446478003,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DwR1gpZjFW9koCDxoGj8rQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"These notes are generic and don't specifically address transformer pad specifications or clearances from the UCM. Let me now compile my final findings. Based on all my research, here are the key deficiencies I've identified:\n\n**DEFINITE FAILS:**\n1. EL-13.31 - No cross-section drawings provided\n2. EL-13.37 - No transformer pad detail sheets provided (no dimensions shown on plans)\n\n**DEFINITE NOT-VERIFIABLE (due to missing information/coordination):**\n1. EL-13.4 - No documentation of AE Design approval for reduced clearances\n2. EL-13.6 - Clearance from windows/doors - equipment type (oil-filled vs dry) not specified\n3. EL-13.7 - Sidewalk clearances - precise distances can't be determined\n4. EL-13.10 - Hot-stick access area 10-foot clearance - no access door orientation shown\n5. EL-13.11 - 15-foot if facing confined space - uncertain if courtyard pads qualify\n6. EL-13.12 - Fire hydrant clearance - visible near one pad but distance unclear\n7. EL-13.13 - Trees utility-compatible - landscape plan doesn't show transformer locations\n8. EL-13.14 - Shrub clearances - landscape plan doesn't coordinate with transformers\n9. EL-13.15 - Root barriers - no coordination between plans\n10. EL-13.17 - Bike rack clearances - distance unclear\n11. EL-13.18 - Light pole clearances - not detailed\n12. EL-13.19 - Fire lane clearances - precise distance unclear\n13. EL-13.20 - 5-foot between transformer pads - 5 pads present, distances not measured\n14. EL-13.21-23 - Utility line clearances (water, wastewater, storm drain) - routing shown but precise distances not detailed\n\n\n15. EL-13.25 - Underground utility separations - not detailed\n16. EL-13.32 - Drainage direction for oil-filled equipment - equipment type not specified\n17. EL-13.34 - Prohibited easement locations - relationship to pads unclear\n18. EL-13.35 - Transformer easements - not shown around pads\n19. EL-13.38 - Bollards - not shown, parking proximity unclear\n\nI should reconsider which items are genuinely missing versus those that don't apply to this project. Some of these standards may not be relevant to the site conditions.\n\n**Items not applicable here:**\n- EL-13.2 - Retaining walls exist on-site (Sheets 38-39) but are positioned at the perimeter and pond areas, not adjacent to transformer locations\n- EL-13.5 - Balconies/overhangs don't apply; the residential townhomes lack shared balcony features\n- EL-13.8 - Stairwells as fire exits aren't shown as independent structures on the plans\n- EL-13.9 - Fire escapes aren't depicted on the residential buildings\n- EL-13.16 - Dumpster placement isn't clearly marked or material to this review\n- EL-13.24 - Gas service doesn't appear on the utility documentation\n- EL-13.27-28 - Overhead distribution lines aren't present; Sheet 21 confirms all electrical runs underground\n- EL-13.29-30 - Niche installations aren't configured on these plans\n\nWait, I should double-check the overhead electric situation. The Austin Energy notes reference both overhead and underground facilities, and Sheet 31 actually shows an \"OHE\" marking along the south property line. That means overhead electric does exist on-site, which could make EL-13.27 and EL-13.28 potentially applicable depending on transformer positioning relative to those overhead conductors. I need to focus on identifying clear failures where required features or documentation are genuinely absent rather than making assumptions about applicability.\n\nLooking at what's objectively missing: cross-section drawings aren't provided for EL-13.31, and transformer pad details with dimensions are absent for EL-13.37. Beyond those definitive gaps, many other items can't be verified because the plans lack specific measurements, equipment specifications, or coordination between different plan sheets. The most significant compliance issues are the ones where documentation is clearly not included rather than where I'm uncertain about applicability.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":67370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44f53564-a2c6-473b-bd29-a0ef36023cf2","uuid":"fb5ca21d-7b92-447c-8692-e0922978ec49"}
