{"level":30,"time":1776446478005,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Carefully examine Electrical Plan Sheet 21 and provide a detailed analysis of each of the 4 transformer pads (labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"). For EACH transformer pad, provide:\n\n1. **SPECIFIC DISTANCE MEASUREMENTS** shown on the plan (in feet or inches) to:\n   - Buildings (measure from edge of pad to nearest building wall)\n   - Sidewalks/pavement\n   - Any adjacent structures\n   - Pull boxes or meters\n   - Any other utilities\n\n2. **DESCRIPTIVE NOTES** visible near or associated with each pad:\n   - Any text callouts about clearances, setbacks, or requirements\n   - Any notes about easements, restricted areas, or special conditions\n   - Any reference to detail sheets or specifications\n\n3. **DIMENSIONS OF THE PADS THEMSELVES** (if shown):\n   - Width and length of each pad\n   - Any equipment sizing information\n\n4. **ACCESS ORIENTATION**:\n   - Can you determine which direction the access door faces on each pad (north, south, east, west)?\n   - Are there dashed clearance boxes or access circles shown around any pads?\n\n5. **EASEMENT INFORMATION**:\n   - Which transformer pads appear to be within or adjacent to easement lines?\n   - What type of easement (Vault, Drainage, etc.)?\n\nProvide EXACT measurements where shown, and note clearly where measurements are ABSENT. Be very specific about what is visible vs. not visible on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21), here is the detailed breakdown of the four locations labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad.\" \n\n**General Observation for all pads:** \nThis specific sheet serves as a preliminary routing plan. It shows the general schematic locations of the electrical infrastructure (using blue lines and symbols) but **does not provide any specific distance measurements, pad dimensions, or clearance boxes for any of the transformer pads.** \n\nHere is the specific analysis for each pad:\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad 1 (Top-Left, near Bldg 1)\n*   **Location:** Located near the top-left curve of the inner site roadway/parking area, northwest of Bldg 1.\n*   **Specific Distance Measurements:** **ABSENT**. There are no dimension lines indicating the distance from the pad to Bldg 1, the adjacent curb, or the nearby pull box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** The only notes pointing to this equipment are the labels \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Pull Box.\" There are no clearance notes, setback requirements, or detail sheet references visible. \n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**. The pad is drawn as a small square, but no length/width dimensions or equipment sizing are provided.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. There are no dashed clearance boxes, access circles, or door indicators to show which way the equipment faces.\n*   **Easement Information:** The pad sits near the edge of the roadway. While there is a \"Wastewater Easement Doc#\" noted further west, no specific utility or vault easement is drawn directly over or pointing to this transformer pad.\n\n### 2. Transformer Pad 2 (Middle-Left, between Bldg 2 & Bldg 8)\n*   **Location:** Located on the western side of the central courtyard area, just south of Bldg 2 and north of Bldg 8.\n*   **Specific Distance Measurements:** **ABSENT**. There are no dimensions provided from the pad to the adjacent buildings, sidewalks, or the adjacent pull box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** The area has leader lines labeling \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and an adjacent \"Electrical Pull Box\". Just south of it, there is a label for \"Underground Electric Line\". No clearance or specification notes are present.\n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. No clearance zones or directional indicators are drawn.\n*   **Easement Information:** This pad is not located within any distinctly marked dashed easement lines on this sheet.\n\n### 3. Transformer Pad 3 (Bottom-Left, south of Bldg 8)\n*   **Location:** Located at the southwest corner of the site's inner loop, directly south of Bldg 8.\n*   **Specific Distance Measurements:** **ABSENT**. There are no dimensions provided to the building, the adjacent sidewalk, or the immediately adjacent pull box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** Labeled with \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Pull Box\". Notably, there is also a leader line reading \"**Vault Easement**\" that points directly to the square representing this transformer pad. \n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. No dashed clearance boxes or access zones are shown.\n*   **Easement Information:** As noted above, a specifically called out \"**Vault Easement**\" is associated directly with this pad location. It is also located immediately adjacent to a dashed line labeled \"**Sidewalk Easement Doc#**\".\n\n### 4. Transformer Pad 4 (Middle-Right, north of Bldg 6)\n*   **Location:** Located on the eastern side of the property, tucked between the eastern boundary line and the area north of Bldg 6 (near unit 604) and east of Bldg 4.\n*   **Specific Distance Measurements:** **ABSENT**. There are no dimensions detailing the distance to Bldg 6, Bldg 4, the eastern property boundary, or the adjacent pull box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** Labeled strictly as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" alongside an \"Electrical Pull Box\". There are no associated clearance rules or detail references.\n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. No access circles or dashed clearance lines are visible.\n*   **Easement Information:** While it is near the eastern property line (which has adjacent off-site 25' Drainage Easements noted), there is no specific P.U.E. or vault easement drawn directly around or pointing to this specific pad on the subject property. \n\n***\n\n**Summary for the Final Review Agent:**\nIf validation requires exact distances (e.g., verifying a minimum 10-foot clearance from a building), pad dimensions, or clearance zones, **that information is not contained on this preliminary electrical routing sheet**. You will need to locate a dedicated \"Site Utility Plan,\" a \"Dimension Control Plan,\" or specific \"Electrical Details\" sheets to find precise measurements and clearance setbacks.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1624,"outputTokens":1076,"totalTokens":4805,"reasoningTokens":2105},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Carefully examine Electrical Plan Sheet 21 and provide a detailed analysis of each of the 4 transformer pads (labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"). For EACH transformer pad, provide:\n\n1. **SPECIFIC DISTANCE MEASUREMENTS** shown on the plan (in feet or inches) to:\n   - Buildings (measure from edge of pad to nearest building wall)\n   - Sidewalks/pavement\n   - Any adjacent structures\n   - Pull boxes or meters\n   - Any other utilities\n\n2. **DESCRIPTIVE NOTES** visible near or associated with each pad:\n   - Any text callouts about clearances, setbacks, or requirements\n   - Any notes about easements, restricted areas, or special conditions\n   - Any reference to detail sheets or specifications\n\n3. **DIMENSIONS OF THE PADS THEMSELVES** (if shown):\n   - Width and length of each pad\n   - Any equipment sizing information\n\n4. **ACCESS ORIENTATION**:\n   - Can you determine which direction the access door faces on each pad (north, south, east, west)?\n   - Are there dashed clearance boxes or access circles shown around any pads?\n\n5. **EASEMENT INFORMATION**:\n   - Which transformer pads appear to be within or adjacent to easement lines?\n   - What type of easement (Vault, Drainage, etc.)?\n\nProvide EXACT measurements where shown, and note clearly where measurements are ABSENT. Be very specific about what is visible vs. not visible on the plan."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-96wQuyssrwk0H065RrwaEiKC","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-mod