ll box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** Labeled with \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Pull Box\". Notably, there is also a leader line reading \"**Vault Easement**\" that points directly to the square representing this transformer pad. \n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. No dashed clearance boxes or access zones are shown.\n*   **Easement Information:** As noted above, a specifically called out \"**Vault Easement**\" is associated directly with this pad location. It is also located immediately adjacent to a dashed line labeled \"**Sidewalk Easement Doc#**\".\n\n### 4. Transformer Pad 4 (Middle-Right, north of Bldg 6)\n*   **Location:** Located on the eastern side of the property, tucked between the eastern boundary line and the area north of Bldg 6 (near unit 604) and east of Bldg 4.\n*   **Specific Distance Measurements:** **ABSENT**. There are no dimensions detailing the distance to Bldg 6, Bldg 4, the eastern property boundary, or the adjacent pull box.\n*   **Descriptive Notes:** Labeled strictly as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" alongside an \"Electrical Pull Box\". There are no associated clearance rules or detail references.\n*   **Dimensions of the Pad:** **ABSENT**.\n*   **Access Orientation:** **Indeterminate**. No access circles or dashed clearance lines are visible.\n*   **Easement Information:** While it is near the eastern property line (which has adjacent off-site 25' Drainage Easements noted), there is no specific P.U.E. or vault easement drawn directly around or pointing to this specific pad on the subject property. \n\n***\n\n**Summary for the Final Review Agent:**\nIf validation requires exact distances (e.g., verifying a minimum 10-foot clearance from a building), pad dimensions, or clearance zones, **that information is not contained on this preliminary electrical routing sheet**. You will need to locate a dedicated \"Site Utility Plan,\" a \"Dimension Control Plan,\" or specific \"Electrical Details\" sheets to find precise measurements and clearance setbacks.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":1091035.580501,"endTime":1120749.529494,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"h2viafSbNs2AjbIPnNSn0Ag"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.04142","marketCost":"0.04142","inferenceCost":"0.04142","inputInferenceCost":"0.003248","outputInferenceCost":"0.038172","generationId":"gen_01KPE782AT8ZPHE19QH60SVFYX"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776446478007,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Search the entire sheet for all notes related to electric utilities, transmission lines, overhead conductors, and any requirement for 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work begins. Also look for notes about tree work near electric lines, easement restrictions, and electric transmission clearances. Read all text carefully.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the exact transcription of all notes related to electric utilities, transmission lines, overhead conductors, tree work near electric lines, easement restrictions, transmission clearances, and notifications to Austin Energy (including the 48-hour notice).\n\n### From the \"General Construction Notes\" Section:\n*   **Item 2:** \"Contractor shall call Texas 811 (811 or 1-800-344-8377) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\"\n\n### From the \"Electric Notes\" Section:\n*   **Item 1:** \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Item 2:** \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Item 3:** \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **Item 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n*   **Item 5:** \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### From the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" Section:\n*   **Item 1:** \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n*   **Item 2:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n*   **Item 3:** \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n*   **Item 4:** \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n*   **Item 5:** \"Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n*   **Item 6:** \"Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n*   **Item 7:** \"No spoils, reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 25 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n*   **Item 8:** \"24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n*   **Item 9:** \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n*   **Item 10:** \"Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n*   **Item 11:** \"Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/powerlines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be doweled curbing.\"\n*   **Item 12:** \"Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n*   **Item 13:** \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n*   **Item 14:** \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n*   **Item 15:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\" *(Note: This appears as a near-duplicate of Item 2 on the plan).*\n*   **Item 16:** \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    *   any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    *   any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected; nor\n    *   any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n### Unnumbered Paragraphs Located Immediately Below the \"Electric Transmission Notes\":\n*(Note: These paragraphs duplicate the text found in the \"Electric Notes\" section above, but are transcribed exactly as they appear at the bottom of the middle column).*\n*   \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n*   \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### From the \"Texas 811\" Callout Box (Bottom Center):\n*   Under the \"Call Before You Dig!!\" logo, there is a disclaimer box that includes: \"...contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1370,"outputTokens":1848,"totalTokens":6171,"reasoningTokens":2953},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Search the entire sheet for all notes related to electric utilities, transmission lines, overhead conductors, and any requirement for 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work begins. Also look for notes about tree work near electric lines, easement restrictions, and electric transmission clearances. Read all text carefully."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-xI7QlPbaliPyqtGfMGDu0uXh","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","a