{"level":30,"time":1776446698766,"pid":76090,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012CxTmbDiNtaTjN2eNTBWfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the evaluation of this grouping. Based on my comprehensive research of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, I identified **8 deficiency findings** across the overhead electric clearance requirements:\n\n## Summary of Findings:\n\n**FAIL Items (3):**\n- **EL-1.7**: Required building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are not provided\n- **EL-1.8**: Required section/plan exhibits with clearance dimension lines are not provided  \n- **EL-1.31**: Required registered surveyor data for pole locations and mid-span clearances is not provided\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items (5):**\n- **EL-1.1**: Building clearances from overhead conductors cannot be verified without surveyed conductor elevations\n- **EL-1.3**: Building projection clearances cannot be verified without section exhibits showing conductor locations\n- **EL-1.18**: Driveway vertical clearances cannot be verified without surveyor mid-span clearance data\n- **EL-1.23**: Cannot verify that clearance dimensions measure from outside conductor versus pole centerline\n- **EL-1.37**: Tree species compliance cannot be verified; trees within 10 feet of overhead utilities lack species identification on landscape plan\n\n## Key Evidence:\n- Overhead electric utilities confirmed on property boundaries (Sheet 4 existing conditions survey)\n- No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor data in site plan set\n- Trees proposed within 10 feet of overhead electric lines per Sheet 31, but species not identified for those locations\n- General notes on Sheet 3 acknowledge owner responsibility for clearances but lack specific dimension verification exhibits\n\nAll 39 other checklist it