pe plan (Sheet 31) shows trees within 10 feet of overhead electric lines marked as mitigation (M) and street yard (SY) trees without species identification on the plan. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists Cedar Elm (not utility-compatible), Live Oak (not utility-compatible), Mexican Redbud (utility-compatible), and Texas Mountain Laurel (utility-compatible), but does not spatially correlate which species are planted in areas within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors. Tree species compliance for those within clearance distances cannot be verified."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"65df8bf4-e4dc-439c-a986-0340648d43c7"}
